WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.900
Hi, welcome back to Arya Nagarjuna.

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.433
This is the review class.

00:00:05.433 --> 00:00:08.166
We've had 14 amazing classes.

00:00:08.166 --> 00:00:12.550
We have gone through,

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:14.492
I think it's nine chapters,

00:00:14.492 --> 00:00:16.980
which is a big achievement
- that's a third.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:19.220
It's not a third of the amount of text,

00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:21.170
but it's a third of the chapters,

00:00:21.170 --> 00:00:22.890
because the chapters
have different lengths,

00:00:22.890 --> 00:00:24.780
and these are shorter chapters.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:28.580
But definitely we've done a huge piece.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:33.220
It's about 20% of the whole
wisdom text of Nagarjuna

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.530
and the commentary by Choney Lama,

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:39.325
which is to say, the
commentary by Tsongkapa also.

00:00:39.325 --> 00:00:41.216
And we made great progress,

00:00:41.216 --> 00:00:42.924
we worked through it very hard.

00:00:42.924 --> 00:00:45.574
And I thought, let's have some fun,

00:00:45.574 --> 00:00:47.099
let's just relax.

00:00:47.099 --> 00:00:50.973
I have seven of my friends here.

00:00:50.973 --> 00:00:53.857
Let's just

00:00:53.857 --> 00:00:58.081
talk about what we just studied.

00:00:58.081 --> 00:01:01.650
And maybe it'd be fun for
you guys at home also,

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:03.592
to listen to us wander

00:01:03.592 --> 00:01:06.433
around in the dark, as they say.

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:08.308
So here we go.

00:01:08.308 --> 00:01:11.657
We started with chapter nine.

00:01:11.657 --> 00:01:15.613
And that's called an investigation

00:01:15.613 --> 00:01:19.020
about who might have been there before.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:21.480
It's a weird name for a chapter.

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:23.221
It's an investigation

00:01:23.221 --> 00:01:26.638
about who might have been there

00:01:26.638 --> 00:01:28.900
before we got there, something like that.

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:31.770
Who might have been there before?

00:01:31.770 --> 00:01:36.770
I'm going to show pictures
and my esteemed friends

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:38.011
are going to guess

00:01:38.011 --> 00:01:41.069
what we were talking about

00:01:41.069 --> 00:01:42.460
with that picture.

00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:44.320
And of course, I would give you clues

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:47.530
because I was careful to
study it before I came.

00:01:47.530 --> 00:01:49.422
Because I also don't remember.

00:01:49.422 --> 00:01:51.321
So here we go.

00:01:51.321 --> 00:01:55.117
First picture, Dr. Pachi.

00:01:55.117 --> 00:01:58.680
Anybody want to explain
briefly what's going on?

00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:02.321
And I'll repeat it for the recording.

00:02:02.321 --> 00:02:07.127
Briefly, what's going on?

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:11.435
There's a young girl. She has a telescope.

00:02:11.435 --> 00:02:12.268
- [Student] She goes outside.

00:02:12.268 --> 00:02:13.927
- She goes outside.

00:02:13.927 --> 00:02:17.010
- [Student] To look at the stars.

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:17.843
- To look at the stars

00:02:17.843 --> 00:02:19.393
but before she looks at the stars,

00:02:19.393 --> 00:02:20.431
Is she an..

00:02:20.431 --> 00:02:21.697
- [Student] Astronomer?

00:02:21.697 --> 00:02:23.967
- Astronomer or not?

00:02:23.967 --> 00:02:24.800
Good, good, good.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:26.583
So which came first?

00:02:26.583 --> 00:02:28.477
The astronomer or the stars?

00:02:28.477 --> 00:02:29.310
It's a joke, right?

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:30.160
- [Student] Yes.

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:32.040
- Yes, she came out first, Geshe-la.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.950
- No, but she wasn't an astronomer yet.

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:36.183
- Why?

00:02:36.183 --> 00:02:38.370
- She wasn't looking at stars yet.

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:40.460
- Wait, so she has to look at stars

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:41.630
before she's astronomer?

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:44.290
- Yes, you cannot call her an astronomer,

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:45.790
until she looks at the stars.

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:48.990
So the stars came first, right?

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:50.620
And then later, she became an astronomer.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:54.387
So she didn't come out of
the house first, right?

00:02:54.387 --> 00:02:57.110
See, this is a problem.

00:02:57.110 --> 00:03:01.489
Because of the wrong way
that we look at reality,

00:03:01.489 --> 00:03:05.290
we are always confused
about how things work.

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:10.187
Always. Even with just somebody

00:03:10.187 --> 00:03:12.843
looking at something, we don't understand.

00:03:12.843 --> 00:03:15.468
And this chapter was

00:03:15.468 --> 00:03:19.776
specifically about the sense powers.

00:03:19.776 --> 00:03:20.940
And how do you look at something?

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:21.900
How do you hear something?

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:22.960
How do you smell something?

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:23.793
How do you taste something?

00:03:23.793 --> 00:03:26.680
How do you feel something?

00:03:26.680 --> 00:03:28.263
Which comes first: the
object or the seeing?

00:03:30.625 --> 00:03:32.940
When you look at a wall,

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:35.160
was the wall there before you looked

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:36.047
or did you open your eyes

00:03:36.047 --> 00:03:38.670
and then the seeds in your mind open,

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:42.620
And then the wall was there to see?

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:45.180
So maybe it's backwards of what we think.

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:48.310
It's not that you open
your eyes and see a wall.

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:53.157
It's that you open your eyes
and make a wall, to see.

00:03:53.157 --> 00:03:55.270
And it doesn't feel like that.

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:57.640
It feels like the wall was there before.

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:00.370
So that can apply to the

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:02.828
Medicine Buddha mantra, for example.

00:04:02.828 --> 00:04:04.128
So you say the mantra,

00:04:04.128 --> 00:04:06.744
and then you think the mantra

00:04:06.744 --> 00:04:10.623
changes somebody's cancer
or something like that.

00:04:10.623 --> 00:04:13.220
So the mantra comes first, right?

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:15.460
And then cure the cancer, right?

00:04:15.460 --> 00:04:18.290
No. Why?

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:21.000
Because until you cure
cancer with some magic words,

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.010
they're not magic words.

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:23.460
They're not mantras.

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:26.384
Mantra means words of power.

00:04:26.384 --> 00:04:27.217
Until they show their power,

00:04:27.217 --> 00:04:29.658
they are not mantras.

00:04:29.658 --> 00:04:34.574
So can you say the mantra
before the cancer is cured?

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:38.600
Can you say a mantra
before the cancer is cured?

00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:40.204
Yes or no?

00:04:40.204 --> 00:04:41.820
No, you cannot.

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:46.303
It's not a mantra until they get cured.

00:04:46.303 --> 00:04:50.290
So you have to think about it.

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:51.923
If Nagarjuna says,

00:04:51.923 --> 00:04:54.739
if you don't understand this point,

00:04:54.739 --> 00:04:56.230
I don't care if you say mantras.

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:58.900
Maybe you get lucky and they cure somebody

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:03.382
because they did something
good 10,000 lifetimes ago.

00:05:03.382 --> 00:05:05.740
But if you want the
mantra to cause the cure,

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:06.573
you have to understand that

00:05:06.573 --> 00:05:08.300
the mantra is not a mantra

00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:09.133
until the cure comes,

00:05:09.133 --> 00:05:10.649
which means the mantra

00:05:10.649 --> 00:05:14.181
is impossible to cause the cure.

00:05:14.181 --> 00:05:15.990
So something else is happening here.

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:19.580
It's not the mantra causes the cure.

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:22.670
Is that your mind creates a mantra,

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:26.473
your mind creates a meditation session,

00:05:26.473 --> 00:05:29.913
and then your mind creates a cancer cure.

00:05:29.913 --> 00:05:34.821
Duck, Duck, Duck.. Not duck, duck, duck.

00:05:34.821 --> 00:05:37.073
So don't do mantras
thinking that the mantras

00:05:37.073 --> 00:05:39.764
are going to cure the person.

00:05:39.764 --> 00:05:42.081
Save life. Protect life.

00:05:42.081 --> 00:05:43.290
Help other people's life.

00:05:43.290 --> 00:05:44.606
I saw a funny thing today.

00:05:44.606 --> 00:05:47.472
I took a picture of it for you.

00:05:47.472 --> 00:05:49.540
There's a new word in the corporate world.

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:52.800
It's called green washing,

00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:55.475
like white washing.

00:05:55.475 --> 00:05:57.349
So in American English,

00:05:57.349 --> 00:06:00.580
white washing means you did something bad,

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:03.640
and then you're white
washing, and it looks good.

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:05.980
And now there's a new
word in corporate world

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:07.570
called green washing.

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:08.811
And it means you take credit

00:06:08.811 --> 00:06:12.228
for carbon sequestering

00:06:12.228 --> 00:06:14.570
that you didn't really do.

00:06:14.570 --> 00:06:17.550
You see what I mean? You say,
oh look, I saved 50 trees.

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:19.152
And somebody says, where's the trees?

00:06:19.152 --> 00:06:19.985
And you're like, well... (looks away),

00:06:19.985 --> 00:06:23.326
and it's called 'green-washing' now.

00:06:23.326 --> 00:06:25.850
It's a new verb in American industry.

00:06:25.850 --> 00:06:28.241
Why am I talking about that?

00:06:28.241 --> 00:06:30.233
It looks like the mantras is causing

00:06:30.233 --> 00:06:34.156
the cancer to go away, but really

00:06:34.156 --> 00:06:38.362
saving lives of animals, for example,

00:06:38.362 --> 00:06:42.870
by saving the environment
and sequestering carbon,

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:45.178
which is a huge saving animals!

00:06:45.178 --> 00:06:47.011
You can save a few fish.

00:06:47.011 --> 00:06:49.870
But what if you save the
whole world's animals?

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:51.670
That would be cool.

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:56.345
Then your mantras will
work to stop cancer.

00:06:56.345 --> 00:06:58.603
Got it?

00:06:58.603 --> 00:07:00.610
Because the mantra comes from you,

00:07:00.610 --> 00:07:02.780
saying the mantra come from you,

00:07:02.780 --> 00:07:04.290
and the cure comes from you.

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:07.740
And it's not that saying
the mantra causes the cure.

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:09.740
Got it?

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:11.440
You have to save life

00:07:11.440 --> 00:07:12.831
before you do the mantra

00:07:12.831 --> 00:07:15.260
or the mantras won't work.

00:07:15.260 --> 00:07:19.156
That's the emptiness of the mantra. Cool.

00:07:19.156 --> 00:07:21.200
That's, by the way, how you can get a cure

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:26.130
before the mantra exists.

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:28.783
Let's go to our next picture.

00:07:28.783 --> 00:07:30.120
By the way that was...

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:34.478
I'm happy that you guys
knew what picture it was.

00:07:34.478 --> 00:07:36.480
This is a tough one, you guys ready?

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:38.430
Oh, I'm on the real one,

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:42.905
let's see here.

00:07:42.905 --> 00:07:46.796
No, I think it's the next one...

00:07:46.796 --> 00:07:51.544
It's a fire.

00:07:51.544 --> 00:07:55.602
(Looking for)

00:07:55.602 --> 00:08:00.338
Good, it's the next picture.

00:08:00.338 --> 00:08:01.604
Now we're on chapter 10,

00:08:01.604 --> 00:08:04.954
which was called?

00:08:04.954 --> 00:08:07.447
If you look at the picture, you can guess,

00:08:07.447 --> 00:08:11.000
"An Investigation of Fire and Firewood."

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:14.766
So now we're on the next chapter.

00:08:14.766 --> 00:08:17.620
And I want to know how chapter 10

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:21.587
is connected to chapter 9, for $100.

00:08:21.587 --> 00:08:23.270
Chapter 10 is

00:08:23.270 --> 00:08:25.395
about fire and firewood.

00:08:25.395 --> 00:08:27.261
Chapter 9 is about

00:08:27.261 --> 00:08:31.894
how does the eye work.

00:08:31.894 --> 00:08:36.804
- [Student] Chapter 10 is about ... burns.

00:08:36.804 --> 00:08:40.690
- Yes, how does fire burn the wood?

00:08:40.690 --> 00:08:42.847
Which is similar to...

00:08:42.847 --> 00:08:45.730
- [Student] Is there an astronomer
before she looks at the stars?

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:49.883
- Yes, roughly. I'll give you 75.

00:08:49.883 --> 00:08:52.760
Here we go.

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:56.410
Chapter 9 was about how
do you see an object;

00:08:56.410 --> 00:08:59.730
how does the subject
interact with the object.

00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:02.220
Chapter 10, if you remember,

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:06.119
who brought up the fire and the firewood?

00:09:06.119 --> 00:09:06.952
- [Student] The other guy...

00:09:06.952 --> 00:09:08.635
- The other guy.

00:09:08.635 --> 00:09:09.468
The other guy,

00:09:09.468 --> 00:09:11.520
he said, look, Nagarjuna,

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:14.645
quit overworking your mind.

00:09:14.645 --> 00:09:16.620
Look, it's simple.

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:19.720
It's the same way that fire burns wood.

00:09:19.720 --> 00:09:22.610
The way that the eye sees the wall

00:09:22.610 --> 00:09:24.910
is the same as the fire burns the wood.

00:09:24.910 --> 00:09:26.710
Why are you make it so complicated?

00:09:26.710 --> 00:09:27.890
And then Nagarjuna says,

00:09:27.890 --> 00:09:29.280
oh you don't think it's complicated

00:09:29.280 --> 00:09:31.280
when you burn the wood with a fire?

00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:33.520
Let me ask you some questions.

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:37.012
So that's why I have this picture

00:09:37.012 --> 00:09:41.861
of people sitting and
doing what to the fire?

00:09:41.861 --> 00:09:44.760
Looking at the fire - I
was trying to bridge you

00:09:44.760 --> 00:09:47.738
from chapter 9 to chapter 10.

00:09:47.738 --> 00:09:50.980
Chapter 9 is about how
do you see the wall.

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:53.246
Chapter 10 is what's really happening

00:09:53.246 --> 00:09:56.829
when fire burns what?

00:09:56.829 --> 00:09:58.350
What kind of wood?

00:09:58.350 --> 00:09:59.183
But before the fire burns the firewood,

00:09:59.183 --> 00:10:02.249
how can you...

00:10:02.249 --> 00:10:04.040
- [Student] The firewood.

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:08.601
- Call it firewood? Duh!

00:10:08.601 --> 00:10:13.384
Let's go to the next one.

00:10:13.384 --> 00:10:18.245
What is the next one?

00:10:18.245 --> 00:10:21.358
No, we're definitely
having a problem here.

00:10:21.358 --> 00:10:25.762
You're not, guys... aren't
showing them in the same order.

00:10:25.762 --> 00:10:29.939
Yes, they should be in the same order.

00:10:29.939 --> 00:10:32.610
- [Student] Oh, by the chapter?

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:34.800
- I think the next one is still in the...

00:10:34.800 --> 00:10:35.633
No, forget chapter numbers,

00:10:35.633 --> 00:10:39.075
stick to the order

00:10:39.075 --> 00:10:43.886
that finder puts them in.

00:10:43.886 --> 00:10:46.550
No, well, I think the next
one is lighting a cigarette.

00:10:46.550 --> 00:10:47.383
I think we're still...

00:10:47.383 --> 00:10:48.216
- [Student] Yes, that's...

00:10:48.216 --> 00:10:51.100
- I'm sorry, I saw a finger.

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:54.990
Here we go.

00:10:54.990 --> 00:10:57.155
Now, I'll give you a clue

00:10:57.155 --> 00:11:01.725
and you tell me what's going on here.

00:11:01.725 --> 00:11:04.291
The flame is not touching the cigarette.

00:11:04.291 --> 00:11:08.249
That's a clue.

00:11:08.249 --> 00:11:12.968
Why did I choose this picture?

00:11:12.968 --> 00:11:15.687
I'll start the conversation.

00:11:15.687 --> 00:11:19.628
Is the fire the firewood or not?

00:11:19.628 --> 00:11:20.860
- [Student] No.

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:24.240
- No, that fire acts
on the firewood, right?

00:11:24.240 --> 00:11:26.840
So let's just confirm.

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:29.382
This is how you do a debate.

00:11:29.382 --> 00:11:31.821
Let's just confirm, no problem.

00:11:31.821 --> 00:11:34.397
We always say no problem.

00:11:34.397 --> 00:11:36.717
Is the fire the firewood?

00:11:36.717 --> 00:11:37.550
- [Student] No.
- No.

00:11:37.550 --> 00:11:42.020
So the fire's acting
on the firewood, right?

00:11:42.020 --> 00:11:44.450
So they're separate things.

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:46.540
You go like this in the
debate [spreads fingers].

00:11:46.540 --> 00:11:49.607
So they're separate things, right?

00:11:49.607 --> 00:11:52.452
Yes or no? Do they have a touch?

00:11:52.452 --> 00:11:54.620
- [Student] No.

00:11:54.620 --> 00:11:58.210
- No! So you can light a cigarette

00:11:58.210 --> 00:12:02.360
by opening a lighter 10,000 miles away,

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:05.440
because they don't have to touch.

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:07.860
So I was trying to find a picture

00:12:07.860 --> 00:12:11.900
that had a little bit of
space between the flame.

00:12:11.900 --> 00:12:14.130
I mean, that space could
be 10 million miles,

00:12:14.130 --> 00:12:15.962
it doesn't matter.

00:12:15.962 --> 00:12:20.179
If the fire is not the cigarette,

00:12:20.179 --> 00:12:22.003
then where do they touch?

00:12:22.003 --> 00:12:23.730
Where can they touch?

00:12:23.730 --> 00:12:25.840
Where's the point of contact

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:28.760
between the cigarette and the fire?

00:12:28.760 --> 00:12:32.420
If they never touch, then you can't light

00:12:32.420 --> 00:12:34.200
a cigarette with the fire.

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:35.966
If they do touch,

00:12:35.966 --> 00:12:39.391
then there's a part of the cause

00:12:39.391 --> 00:12:43.100
which touches the result. Am I right?

00:12:43.100 --> 00:12:46.317
And in that case, something in the past

00:12:46.317 --> 00:12:50.323
which is already gone can
affect something in the present.

00:12:50.323 --> 00:12:52.737
- [Student] Definitely.

00:12:52.737 --> 00:12:55.512
- No, it's gone.

00:12:55.512 --> 00:12:57.253
If it's gone for a millisecond

00:12:57.253 --> 00:12:58.320
or it's gone for a million years.

00:12:58.320 --> 00:12:59.153
it doesn't matter.

00:12:59.153 --> 00:13:01.103
It's gone. It can't do anything.

00:13:01.103 --> 00:13:03.400
Something in the past
can't burn your finger

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:08.283
and it cannot light a cigarette.

00:13:08.283 --> 00:13:12.742
Or else do they exist
at the same time? Hmm.

00:13:12.742 --> 00:13:15.950
Anyway, what's the point Geshe-la?

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:17.350
Why are we talking about all this stuff?

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:18.870
Let me do my Medicine Buddha mantras,

00:13:18.870 --> 00:13:19.703
don't hassle me.

00:13:19.703 --> 00:13:21.828
I'm trying to say,

00:13:21.828 --> 00:13:22.661
by the time you finish the mantra,

00:13:22.661 --> 00:13:25.861
it's gone.

00:13:25.861 --> 00:13:28.346
And it cannot cure cancer.

00:13:28.346 --> 00:13:30.396
Something from a million years ago

00:13:30.396 --> 00:13:32.779
cannot cure cancer.

00:13:32.779 --> 00:13:36.980
And something from one
half of a second ago

00:13:36.980 --> 00:13:38.546
cannot cure cancer

00:13:38.546 --> 00:13:41.988
because it's gone and it doesn't exist.

00:13:41.988 --> 00:13:43.913
And it can't touch anything,

00:13:43.913 --> 00:13:46.754
if it's not here.

00:13:46.754 --> 00:13:47.587
Mantras cannot cure cancer.

00:13:47.587 --> 00:13:50.720
It can't be like that.

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:51.760
- Oh, Geshe-la,

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:52.993
I heard many stories.

00:13:52.993 --> 00:13:55.017
People cured their cancer

00:13:55.017 --> 00:13:55.850
by saying mantras.

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:59.767
- No, your mind created a person seeing...

00:13:59.767 --> 00:14:00.960
talking a mantra.

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:01.793
Your mind created the sound.

00:14:01.793 --> 00:14:04.468
Then your mind created

00:14:04.468 --> 00:14:05.990
the cancer being caused.

00:14:05.990 --> 00:14:08.373
If you want to cure cancer,

00:14:08.373 --> 00:14:09.981
good, say mantras.

00:14:09.981 --> 00:14:12.030
But first collect the karma.

00:14:12.030 --> 00:14:13.030
What's the karma?

00:14:13.030 --> 00:14:15.963
Sequester carbon,

00:14:15.963 --> 00:14:17.896
save a billion animals,

00:14:17.896 --> 00:14:18.729
save 780 billion animals,

00:14:18.729 --> 00:14:21.012
I think ,I looked it up

00:14:21.012 --> 00:14:23.670
something, in the world.

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:26.403
So if you fix the over...

00:14:26.403 --> 00:14:28.244
what do you call it?..

00:14:28.244 --> 00:14:30.888
overheating problem with the atmosphere?

00:14:30.888 --> 00:14:32.260
- [Student] Climate change?

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:35.101
- Climate change...

00:14:35.101 --> 00:14:37.775
Then you're going to save maybe

00:14:37.775 --> 00:14:39.430
about 50 billion animals. Let's do that.

00:14:39.430 --> 00:14:41.980
Then you can say mantras,
everything will happen.

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:43.840
All kinds of weird stuff will happen.

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:46.710
Geshe-la will get croissants
every five minutes.

00:14:46.710 --> 00:14:49.780
Impossible things.

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:53.244
Next picture.

00:14:53.244 --> 00:14:57.280
Is it.. What is this?

00:14:57.280 --> 00:15:00.510
And be prepared to prove it.

00:15:00.510 --> 00:15:02.648
What's in the picture?

00:15:02.648 --> 00:15:04.280
- [Student] Its a  bundle of firewood.

00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:05.950
- Yeah, why is it firewood?

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:09.450
- [Student] Firewood is not
firewood until it starts fire.

00:15:09.450 --> 00:15:12.860
- Until you start a fire. Until it burns.

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:14.460
Therefore this cannot be firewood

00:15:14.460 --> 00:15:16.846
because it hasn't burned yet, right?

00:15:16.846 --> 00:15:18.410
(laughing)

00:15:18.410 --> 00:15:21.090
Same thing, don't get confused.

00:15:21.090 --> 00:15:23.660
By the way, we're still in what chapter?

00:15:23.660 --> 00:15:28.274
Chapter 10, we're still
investigating firewood.

00:15:28.274 --> 00:15:31.950
Nagarjuna spends a lot
of time on chapter 10.

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:34.640
It seems to be important to him.

00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:35.914
Alright,

00:15:35.914 --> 00:15:40.914
let's look at our next picture.

00:15:40.917 --> 00:15:45.917
We're still in chapter 10.

00:15:45.929 --> 00:15:50.929
And

00:15:50.936 --> 00:15:55.230
we're talking about dependent origination.

00:15:55.230 --> 00:15:57.930
What's the short way to
describe dependent origination?

00:15:57.930 --> 00:16:00.360
What was the first thing Lord Buddha said,

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:02.048
when he taught dependent origination?

00:16:02.048 --> 00:16:03.000
- (indistinct)

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:05.590
Yes, if this happens, then that happens.

00:16:05.590 --> 00:16:08.060
He didn't say there's 12 links or the law.

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:09.567
Well, he didn't say that, he said

00:16:09.567 --> 00:16:12.400
Look: if this happens, that happens.

00:16:12.400 --> 00:16:15.130
He was probably going
like this [shows gesture]:

00:16:15.130 --> 00:16:19.310
If this happens, that happens, get it?

00:16:19.310 --> 00:16:21.030
That's dependent origination.

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:23.888
Later, they put a big name on it.

00:16:23.888 --> 00:16:27.187
But the very first time he
explained it, it was like,

00:16:27.187 --> 00:16:30.012
if this happens, then
that's going to happen.

00:16:30.012 --> 00:16:32.450
It's just like what your mom used to say,

00:16:32.450 --> 00:16:36.010
if you do this, you're
going to have that happen.

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:38.350
Your mom tried to teach you.

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:39.920
So that's cause and effect.

00:16:39.920 --> 00:16:44.110
So what that means is: think about it.

00:16:44.110 --> 00:16:46.950
The second thing to happen,

00:16:46.950 --> 00:16:49.750
depends on the first
thing to happen. Got it?

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:52.120
If you do this, this is going to happen.

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:54.430
Now, if you talk about dependence,

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:55.890
the second thing to happen

00:16:55.890 --> 00:16:58.680
is depending on the first thing to happen.

00:16:58.680 --> 00:17:02.480
It's like: here's the coffee cup

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:04.130
and here's the handkerchief.

00:17:04.130 --> 00:17:08.879
So this is the thing that happened,

00:17:08.879 --> 00:17:10.495
and this is the cause.

00:17:10.495 --> 00:17:12.700
The cause supports the result, right?

00:17:12.700 --> 00:17:16.790
If you do this, honey, you're
going to get that, honey.

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:19.650
Okay, because that depends
on this, doing this.

00:17:19.650 --> 00:17:21.800
Getting that depends on doing this. Right?

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:24.870
So there's a dependent relationship.

00:17:24.870 --> 00:17:28.620
Results rest on causes. Right?

00:17:28.620 --> 00:17:31.590
- No, by the time the result comes out,

00:17:31.590 --> 00:17:34.160
the cause is long gone.

00:17:34.160 --> 00:17:36.540
There's no such thing as dependence.

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:39.554
You can cancel all the
Sugeng's translations.

00:17:39.554 --> 00:17:40.395
(laughing)

00:17:40.395 --> 00:17:43.162
It's all impossible.

00:17:43.162 --> 00:17:44.560
Why?

00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:49.220
Because to have dependence,
that thing that happens second

00:17:49.220 --> 00:17:52.120
have to depend on the
thing that happens first.

00:17:52.120 --> 00:17:55.150
And if the thing that happens
first is already gone,

00:17:55.150 --> 00:17:58.067
then there's no dependence,

00:17:58.067 --> 00:18:01.740
just the handkerchief
falls on the floor. Got it?

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:03.550
All right, so that's what it really means.

00:18:03.550 --> 00:18:06.690
So where's the dependence?

00:18:06.690 --> 00:18:09.950
Now $100 question. Let's
go to that last picture,

00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:13.411
the parts of the pen.

00:18:13.411 --> 00:18:17.395
I say something is depending
on something in this picture.

00:18:17.395 --> 00:18:20.890
I say something is depending on something

00:18:20.890 --> 00:18:23.259
in this picture, for $100.

00:18:23.259 --> 00:18:25.210
(indistinct chattering)

00:18:25.210 --> 00:18:27.993
Somebody tell me what's depending on what?

00:18:27.993 --> 00:18:30.380
- [Student] The pen is depending on table.

00:18:30.380 --> 00:18:34.386
- I thought you'd say that.
Anybody else want to try?

00:18:34.386 --> 00:18:36.690
- [Student] Maybe it depends on the seeds.

00:18:36.690 --> 00:18:40.110
- Yes, good, $100 for Pachi.

00:18:40.110 --> 00:18:42.250
Yeah, the pen depends on the seeds.

00:18:42.250 --> 00:18:44.530
This is a trick picture.

00:18:44.530 --> 00:18:47.110
This picture is a trick.
Geshe-la is going to say,

00:18:47.110 --> 00:18:49.340
"Oh, what's depending on what?"

00:18:49.340 --> 00:18:51.670
And Gyelse is going to say, "Oh
the pen depends on the table,"

00:18:51.670 --> 00:18:52.770
and then Pachi can say,

00:18:52.770 --> 00:18:57.380
"No, the pen is depending
on my seed." Got it?

00:18:57.380 --> 00:19:00.779
That's all. That was a clever picture.

00:19:00.779 --> 00:19:03.321
I guess, I don't know.

00:19:03.321 --> 00:19:07.970
After I die, who's going to
remember what this picture is?

00:19:07.970 --> 00:19:10.344
All right, (laughing)

00:19:10.344 --> 00:19:14.890
Here we go next one.

00:19:14.890 --> 00:19:18.010
Wait, man, isn't there...

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:23.010
And maybe I'm in the wrong place.

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:27.760
Let me check that one

00:19:27.760 --> 00:19:32.756
(Murmuring)

00:19:32.756 --> 00:19:37.697
Wow, this is really weird.

00:19:37.697 --> 00:19:41.213
(silence)

00:19:41.213 --> 00:19:44.220
(silence)

00:19:44.220 --> 00:19:46.440
Okay, we got the bundle of firewood,

00:19:46.440 --> 00:19:48.960
we got the pen on the desk.

00:19:48.960 --> 00:19:53.480
Oh, right, you're right. Okay, good.

00:19:53.480 --> 00:19:58.480
The other guys said, look, you can see

00:19:58.490 --> 00:20:02.110
that the fire comes from the firewood.

00:20:02.110 --> 00:20:05.120
For example: Look,
Nagarjuna, I don't care,

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:07.650
if you say the fire is the firewood,

00:20:07.650 --> 00:20:10.870
or you say the fire is
separate from the firewood.

00:20:10.870 --> 00:20:12.410
It doesn't really matter.

00:20:12.410 --> 00:20:16.170
If you put a match on some
dry wood, it's going to burn.

00:20:16.170 --> 00:20:20.194
Now, I don't care what kind
of philosophy you have.

00:20:20.194 --> 00:20:23.400
I can burn your house down. Watch me.

00:20:23.400 --> 00:20:27.070
Then you can philosophize about it.

00:20:27.070 --> 00:20:31.110
But anyone can see that
when you put a match

00:20:31.110 --> 00:20:34.304
near a bunch of dry stuff, it burns.

00:20:34.304 --> 00:20:39.204
And then Nagarjuna
replies with this picture.

00:20:39.204 --> 00:20:43.006
What's the point of the picture?

00:20:43.006 --> 00:20:48.006
(indistinct)

00:20:48.013 --> 00:20:51.162
Well, I'm saying...

00:20:51.162 --> 00:20:53.696
Why did I use colored glasses here?

00:20:53.696 --> 00:20:56.912
(indistinct)

00:20:56.912 --> 00:20:59.484
Yes, just because you see it
that way, it doesn't mean...

00:20:59.484 --> 00:21:00.323
- [Student] that it's correct.

00:21:00.323 --> 00:21:03.560
- That it's correct, yes, your eyes are...

00:21:03.560 --> 00:21:05.060
Your equipment is broken.

00:21:05.060 --> 00:21:07.290
That would be Nagarjuna's answer.

00:21:07.290 --> 00:21:10.180
In fact, listen to this:

00:21:10.180 --> 00:21:13.510
everything in the Wheel
of Life is broken. Got it?

00:21:13.510 --> 00:21:16.300
And it took me many
years to figure that out.

00:21:16.300 --> 00:21:20.320
If something is painted
in the Wheel of Life,

00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:23.310
inside the wheel, inside
the edges of the wheel,

00:21:23.310 --> 00:21:25.930
it's broken.

00:21:25.930 --> 00:21:29.630
Everything there is effed up, everything.

00:21:29.630 --> 00:21:32.029
So

00:21:32.029 --> 00:21:35.660
your eyes, which are LNGA PA SKYE MCHED,

00:21:35.660 --> 00:21:37.850
fifth link.

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:41.370
The buildings, empty
buildings - they are broken.

00:21:41.370 --> 00:21:43.580
They are broken. Your eyes are broken.

00:21:43.580 --> 00:21:48.238
Don't tell me fire burns wood

00:21:48.238 --> 00:21:51.760
because I can see it.

00:21:51.760 --> 00:21:55.502
Is everything pink in the world?

00:21:55.502 --> 00:21:58.060
Is my white phone pink?

00:21:58.060 --> 00:22:00.350
Why? Why are you saying that, Geshe-la?

00:22:00.350 --> 00:22:02.910
Because if you have pink eyeglasses on,

00:22:02.910 --> 00:22:05.720
it's going to look pink to you.

00:22:05.720 --> 00:22:07.960
And you always have these eyeglasses on.

00:22:07.960 --> 00:22:10.210
You are born with these sunglasses on.

00:22:10.210 --> 00:22:12.350
And you will wear them
until the day they die.

00:22:12.350 --> 00:22:16.110
You are born with a defect in your eye.

00:22:16.110 --> 00:22:19.115
What's the famous example
about a defect in your eye?

00:22:19.115 --> 00:22:20.310
- [Student] Cataract?

00:22:20.310 --> 00:22:23.330
- Yes, which kind of means
you have a scratch on your eye

00:22:23.330 --> 00:22:25.320
on your cornea.

00:22:25.320 --> 00:22:27.046
And you think there's some -

00:22:27.046 --> 00:22:28.217
- [Student] Hair on sink.

00:22:28.217 --> 00:22:30.440
- Or you think there's a crack in
the porcelain. You see, get it?

00:22:30.440 --> 00:22:34.150
And it's really just a
scratch on your eyeball.

00:22:34.150 --> 00:22:37.490
So, according to Buddhism,

00:22:37.490 --> 00:22:40.520
of course your mind is
misunderstanding everything.

00:22:40.520 --> 00:22:42.670
But the problem is worse than that.

00:22:42.670 --> 00:22:47.080
Your eyeball is broken.

00:22:47.080 --> 00:22:49.580
You always see things the wrong way.

00:22:49.580 --> 00:22:52.238
When you think you see
a match causing a fire

00:22:52.238 --> 00:22:56.063
or when you think a
mantra is curing cancer,

00:22:56.063 --> 00:22:57.379
you are...

00:22:57.379 --> 00:23:00.454
There's a problem with your eyes.

00:23:00.454 --> 00:23:02.480
That's not what's happening.

00:23:02.480 --> 00:23:04.520
What's really happening Geshe-la?

00:23:04.520 --> 00:23:07.420
You saved a bunch of animals
live by, I don't know,

00:23:07.420 --> 00:23:10.120
planting a forest in Diamond Mountain.

00:23:10.120 --> 00:23:12.770
Then that oxygen saved many animals.

00:23:12.770 --> 00:23:17.550
And then you did mantras and
you can cure cancer. Got it?

00:23:17.550 --> 00:23:19.141
That's all.

00:23:19.141 --> 00:23:21.440
If Nagarjuna is correct,

00:23:21.440 --> 00:23:26.273
we have to be nice to animals
and other humans as well.

00:23:26.273 --> 00:23:30.476
All right, next one,

00:23:30.476 --> 00:23:35.471
(singing)

00:23:35.471 --> 00:23:40.470
(silence)

00:23:40.470 --> 00:23:42.344
This picture is connected to this.

00:23:42.344 --> 00:23:47.100
For $100, tell me why?

00:23:47.100 --> 00:23:49.726
This picture is connected to this..

00:23:49.726 --> 00:23:51.710
[Student] Fire, cook, pizza

00:23:51.710 --> 00:23:54.859
Yes, good, $100 for the young man.

00:23:54.859 --> 00:23:57.200
You are just self-reporting, okay,

00:23:57.200 --> 00:24:01.080
if you don't report it's not my problem.

00:24:01.080 --> 00:24:04.000
At what point is the pizza done?

00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:06.700
At what point is the pizza done?

00:24:06.700 --> 00:24:08.240
At what point?

00:24:08.240 --> 00:24:11.810
So there's past fire, there's future fire.

00:24:11.810 --> 00:24:13.820
And there's the fire in the moment.

00:24:13.820 --> 00:24:17.080
And that keeps moving, the
present moment keeps moving.

00:24:17.080 --> 00:24:19.110
What is the perfect point?

00:24:19.110 --> 00:24:23.840
What cooked the pizza
perfectly, by the way?

00:24:23.840 --> 00:24:26.860
You've made dinner for
somebody else two weeks ago,

00:24:26.860 --> 00:24:31.021
and you didn't burn it.

00:24:31.021 --> 00:24:32.847
You made dinner for somebody two weeks ago

00:24:32.847 --> 00:24:34.140
you didn't burn it.

00:24:34.140 --> 00:24:36.500
Then you went to Rotten
Johnny's and bought a pizza

00:24:36.500 --> 00:24:38.010
and it was perfect.

00:24:38.010 --> 00:24:38.843
Why?

00:24:38.843 --> 00:24:42.390
He found the impossible
line between undercooked

00:24:42.390 --> 00:24:44.200
and overcooked.

00:24:44.200 --> 00:24:48.180
Where's the line between
undercooked and overcooked?

00:24:48.180 --> 00:24:50.640
Where does the part of the room

00:24:50.640 --> 00:24:52.310
you walked on already

00:24:52.310 --> 00:24:55.030
meet the part of the room
you didn't walk on already?

00:24:55.030 --> 00:24:57.720
Because they're both gone.

00:24:57.720 --> 00:25:00.450
One happened already.
One hasn't happened yet.

00:25:00.450 --> 00:25:01.760
They're not there.

00:25:01.760 --> 00:25:02.830
Where do they meet?

00:25:02.830 --> 00:25:07.510
They can't meet anywhere,
they're not here in the room.

00:25:07.510 --> 00:25:09.100
It's all coming from you.

00:25:09.100 --> 00:25:10.833
When you walk through a door,

00:25:10.833 --> 00:25:14.049
what's really happening?

00:25:14.049 --> 00:25:14.899
[Student] Pictures...

00:25:14.899 --> 00:25:17.690
Yes. Small picture. Bigger picture.

00:25:17.690 --> 00:25:21.380
Tape up the doorframe. Small
picture, bigger picture,

00:25:21.380 --> 00:25:24.230
bigger picture, bigger picture,
small picture, small picture.

00:25:24.230 --> 00:25:27.900
I read a nice book once, Ursula Le Guin.

00:25:27.900 --> 00:25:32.410
It's a short story. It's about
a tree that got overworked.

00:25:32.410 --> 00:25:33.980
Why?

00:25:33.980 --> 00:25:37.300
It's a very old tree. It's
like a 500 year old tree.

00:25:37.300 --> 00:25:42.090
In the old days, when
people walked or had wagons,

00:25:42.090 --> 00:25:44.712
life was bearable.

00:25:44.712 --> 00:25:46.010
What do you mean?

00:25:46.010 --> 00:25:49.080
Well, as they got closer
to me, I had to grow.

00:25:49.080 --> 00:25:51.130
And then as they walked
away, I had to shrink.

00:25:51.130 --> 00:25:54.370
And, you know, I was okay,
but now 80 miles an hour.

00:25:54.370 --> 00:25:56.320
How the goddamn they expect me to grow

00:25:56.320 --> 00:26:00.300
and shrink in a 1/10th of a second?

00:26:00.300 --> 00:26:03.860
It's too stressful. The
tree was complaining about

00:26:03.860 --> 00:26:05.303
I have to grow as they get closer

00:26:05.303 --> 00:26:08.160
and I have to shrink really
fast as the drive away...

00:26:08.160 --> 00:26:10.983
It's too much. It's too fast.

00:26:10.983 --> 00:26:14.900
That's what's really
happening. Thank you tree.

00:26:14.900 --> 00:26:17.917
Alright, here we go.

00:26:17.917 --> 00:26:22.850
(silence)

00:26:22.850 --> 00:26:26.910
And what's the favorite...

00:26:26.910 --> 00:26:28.370
What do you call it?

00:26:28.370 --> 00:26:32.553
It's not bitching, it's similar?

00:26:32.553 --> 00:26:36.103
Geshe-la is always kvetching.
Yes, kvetching is good.

00:26:36.103 --> 00:26:37.369
Geshe-la is always...

00:26:37.369 --> 00:26:40.210
Geshe-la is always making some statement

00:26:40.210 --> 00:26:41.810
regarding a turtle.

00:26:41.810 --> 00:26:45.880
For $100 who can tell me?

00:26:45.880 --> 00:26:48.070
What's the statement
Geshe-la likes to make about

00:26:48.070 --> 00:26:52.622
this particular turtle?

00:26:52.622 --> 00:26:55.115
- [Student] That, if you think that

00:26:55.115 --> 00:26:59.924
the world is carrying... on the...

00:26:59.924 --> 00:27:01.198
- On the back?

00:27:01.198 --> 00:27:03.700
- [Student] (indistinct) the
turtle, then that means that

00:27:03.700 --> 00:27:05.939
- everything inside the world

00:27:05.939 --> 00:27:07.243
- they think how it was made is wrong.

00:27:07.243 --> 00:27:11.883
- Good, yeah. $100 for you,
don't forget to tell my boss.

00:27:11.883 --> 00:27:16.883
So, I don't know, 3000 years ago in India,

00:27:16.889 --> 00:27:18.470
people believe the whole world

00:27:18.470 --> 00:27:21.495
was being held up by a turtle.

00:27:21.495 --> 00:27:23.080
that it was flat,

00:27:23.080 --> 00:27:25.840
and it was being held up by a turtle.

00:27:25.840 --> 00:27:30.840
If you misunderstand

00:27:30.840 --> 00:27:34.000
how the whole world happened,

00:27:34.000 --> 00:27:37.290
then you misunderstand
everything in your life.

00:27:37.290 --> 00:27:40.214
If you misunderstand

00:27:40.214 --> 00:27:42.850
how fire burns wood,

00:27:42.850 --> 00:27:46.500
then you must misunderstand
mantras, for example.

00:27:46.500 --> 00:27:48.820
You must. You have to.

00:27:48.820 --> 00:27:52.320
And I give you a possibility.

00:27:52.320 --> 00:27:54.630
How many people in ancient India

00:27:54.630 --> 00:27:58.830
understood the shape of the world,

00:27:58.830 --> 00:28:02.480
correctly? Zero, Zero.

00:28:02.480 --> 00:28:04.227
Call it 10 million, 50 million,

00:28:04.227 --> 00:28:06.740
I don't know how many
were alive at that time.

00:28:06.740 --> 00:28:09.928
How many percent of them are wrong?

00:28:09.928 --> 00:28:12.570
100%. 100%.

00:28:12.570 --> 00:28:16.136
So, in theory, it's possible

00:28:16.136 --> 00:28:19.262
that we are also wrong 100%.

00:28:19.262 --> 00:28:24.262
It has happened in the past
that people had the wrong idea

00:28:24.262 --> 00:28:27.703
about how much stuff?

00:28:27.703 --> 00:28:29.210
Everything.

00:28:29.210 --> 00:28:32.580
You got to say it like that: everything.

00:28:32.580 --> 00:28:36.222
And maybe we were also wrong about

00:28:36.222 --> 00:28:38.750
everything.

00:28:38.750 --> 00:28:42.760
So then, if you're wrong about fires,

00:28:42.760 --> 00:28:45.520
or you're wrong about how plants grow,

00:28:45.520 --> 00:28:49.330
or you're wrong about how
your husband yells at you,

00:28:49.330 --> 00:28:50.860
then maybe you're wrong about everything.

00:28:50.860 --> 00:28:52.400
Wives are wrong more than husbands.

00:28:52.400 --> 00:28:56.131
Can I say it Pachi? I think it's true.

00:28:56.131 --> 00:28:59.202
Just kidding.

00:28:59.202 --> 00:29:00.080
(laughing)

00:29:00.080 --> 00:29:02.300
It's always the husband
in the kitchen, right?

00:29:02.300 --> 00:29:04.291
Anyway,

00:29:04.291 --> 00:29:07.830
just consider the possibility:

00:29:07.830 --> 00:29:10.070
if Nagarjuna is correct in this book,

00:29:10.070 --> 00:29:14.940
if this book is correct, then
everything you think is wrong.

00:29:14.940 --> 00:29:18.840
And that means every action

00:29:18.840 --> 00:29:22.920
you ever took in your life is wrong.

00:29:22.920 --> 00:29:26.550
When you turn the switch
to turn on this light,

00:29:26.550 --> 00:29:30.900
it was a mistake. That was
based on a misunderstanding.

00:29:30.900 --> 00:29:33.508
When you turn the key to start your car,

00:29:33.508 --> 00:29:37.577
you're insane.

00:29:37.577 --> 00:29:39.270
(laughing)

00:29:39.270 --> 00:29:42.676
You should be looking for
someone to give a ride.

00:29:42.676 --> 00:29:45.740
Then try to start your car.

00:29:45.740 --> 00:29:48.960
Otherwise your car
might not start someday,

00:29:48.960 --> 00:29:52.410
which of course never happens.

00:29:52.410 --> 00:29:55.917
Next one.

00:29:55.917 --> 00:30:00.158
(silence)

00:30:00.158 --> 00:30:01.670
This picture... by the way,

00:30:01.670 --> 00:30:04.450
we're on to chapter 11.

00:30:04.450 --> 00:30:05.550
So this is the third

00:30:05.550 --> 00:30:06.508
chapter we've worked on.

00:30:06.508 --> 00:30:07.733
By the way, not every class

00:30:07.733 --> 00:30:08.683
was a separate chapters,

00:30:08.683 --> 00:30:10.404
some classes took...

00:30:10.404 --> 00:30:12.850
some chapters took more than one class.

00:30:12.850 --> 00:30:14.695
But we did chapter 11.

00:30:14.695 --> 00:30:16.403
Chapter 11 is called an

00:30:16.403 --> 00:30:18.410
investigation of a first beginning

00:30:18.410 --> 00:30:20.410
and a final ending to things.

00:30:20.410 --> 00:30:22.160
Is there a first beginning

00:30:22.160 --> 00:30:24.340
and is there a final ending to things.

00:30:24.340 --> 00:30:27.420
When they asked Lord Buddha,

00:30:27.420 --> 00:30:28.560
"Did the universe have...

00:30:28.560 --> 00:30:29.930
did sansara have a beginning?

00:30:29.930 --> 00:30:30.871
Does sansara have an end?

00:30:30.871 --> 00:30:32.129
What did he's say?

00:30:32.129 --> 00:30:33.580
[Student] (Indistinct)

00:30:33.580 --> 00:30:35.500
What do you say?

00:30:35.500 --> 00:30:39.325
Well, yeah, but then...

00:30:39.325 --> 00:30:40.525
What was the question?

00:30:40.525 --> 00:30:43.230
They didn't say 'is there', they said...

00:30:43.230 --> 00:30:44.870
- [Student] Did you see?

00:30:44.870 --> 00:30:47.370
- Yeah, is it evident to you?

00:30:47.370 --> 00:30:50.850
MNGON PA - is it evident to you?

00:30:50.850 --> 00:30:52.583
And so this picture

00:30:52.583 --> 00:30:57.583
is meant to describe...

00:30:58.040 --> 00:30:59.698
If you ask me, does everything

00:30:59.698 --> 00:31:00.710
have a beginning?

00:31:00.710 --> 00:31:03.145
I can answer you on two levels.

00:31:03.145 --> 00:31:04.270
If you ask me, does

00:31:04.270 --> 00:31:06.077
everything have a beginning?

00:31:06.077 --> 00:31:08.050
I can answer you on two levels.

00:31:08.050 --> 00:31:10.880
On an obvious level, I can say no,

00:31:10.880 --> 00:31:12.400
because everything has a cause.

00:31:12.400 --> 00:31:13.660
Therefore nothing has...

00:31:13.660 --> 00:31:14.493
There is no beginning

00:31:14.493 --> 00:31:15.820
to everything.

00:31:15.820 --> 00:31:20.495
On a deeper level,

00:31:20.495 --> 00:31:25.313
why do we think anything begins?

00:31:26.670 --> 00:31:29.301
When did this class begin?

00:31:29.301 --> 00:31:32.810
About 100 years ago.

00:31:32.810 --> 00:31:37.753
When did this class begin?

00:31:38.838 --> 00:31:42.240
When the seeds in your mind open.

00:31:42.240 --> 00:31:45.130
This class, on a deeper level

00:31:45.130 --> 00:31:48.556
this class had no beginning.

00:31:48.556 --> 00:31:50.756
The class didn't start.

00:31:50.756 --> 00:31:53.120
Your seeds opened. Got it?

00:31:53.120 --> 00:31:55.240
Don't ask me did the class start?

00:31:55.240 --> 00:31:56.073
Don't ask me how

00:31:56.073 --> 00:31:57.360
long ago the class started.

00:31:57.360 --> 00:31:58.193
Did you notice I'm not

00:31:58.193 --> 00:31:59.918
using the timer anymore?

00:31:59.918 --> 00:32:00.896
I don't care.

00:32:00.896 --> 00:32:02.020
(laughing)

00:32:02.020 --> 00:32:02.961
Don't ask me when

00:32:02.961 --> 00:32:05.003
the class started. I don't care.

00:32:05.003 --> 00:32:06.660
The class started when your seeds open.

00:32:06.660 --> 00:32:07.790
You can answer your own question.

00:32:07.790 --> 00:32:09.097
Don't ask me how many minutes went by.

00:32:09.097 --> 00:32:11.100
That's not the answer.

00:32:11.100 --> 00:32:12.260
That's why Buddha,

00:32:12.260 --> 00:32:13.093
when they asked him

00:32:13.093 --> 00:32:16.750
this question originally, he said...

00:32:16.750 --> 00:32:20.183
What was his first
answer to this question?

00:32:20.183 --> 00:32:22.090
LUNG MA BSTAN

00:32:23.190 --> 00:32:24.665
Well, that means he

00:32:24.665 --> 00:32:27.310
refused to answer.

00:32:27.310 --> 00:32:28.690
Don't ask stupid questions.

00:32:28.690 --> 00:32:29.523
Hey, Geshe-la,

00:32:29.523 --> 00:32:30.670
what time did the class start?

00:32:30.670 --> 00:32:31.503
How many minutes ago

00:32:31.503 --> 00:32:32.428
did the the class start?

00:32:32.428 --> 00:32:34.293
Don't ask me a stupid question.

00:32:34.293 --> 00:32:35.650
Why is this a stupid question?

00:32:35.650 --> 00:32:37.820
It started when your seeds opened. Got it?

00:32:37.820 --> 00:32:41.410
Don't blame me. You created the class.

00:32:41.410 --> 00:32:42.243
It's your problem.

00:32:42.243 --> 00:32:44.076
If it goes on too long,

00:32:44.076 --> 00:32:46.243
that's your fault.

00:32:46.243 --> 00:32:50.035
Go to the bathroom and

00:32:50.035 --> 00:32:51.112
yell at the mirror.

00:32:51.112 --> 00:32:52.470
(laughing)

00:32:52.470 --> 00:32:54.136
That's the DCI. Probably I have

00:32:54.136 --> 00:32:57.569
to pay a commission to DCI now.

00:32:57.569 --> 00:33:02.553
Okay, just kidding. What's next?

00:33:07.500 --> 00:33:10.340
This was described as the difference

00:33:10.340 --> 00:33:11.890
between making something out of nothing

00:33:11.890 --> 00:33:13.740
and making something out of something.

00:33:13.740 --> 00:33:16.823
Everything is artificial.

00:33:16.823 --> 00:33:18.450
The world is artificial.

00:33:18.450 --> 00:33:20.118
There is nothing real.

00:33:20.118 --> 00:33:23.438
How much of the world is artificial?

00:33:23.438 --> 00:33:25.520
Everything.

00:33:25.520 --> 00:33:26.880
So is it empty?

00:33:26.880 --> 00:33:27.713
Yes.

00:33:27.713 --> 00:33:28.546
Does it exist?

00:33:28.546 --> 00:33:29.379
Yes.

00:33:29.379 --> 00:33:30.580
Is it real?

00:33:30.580 --> 00:33:31.646
Well, yeah, I mean,

00:33:31.646 --> 00:33:33.513
go out and stand in front of a car

00:33:33.513 --> 00:33:35.768
and tell me what happens.

00:33:35.768 --> 00:33:39.530
It's still breaking. But in the one sense

00:33:39.530 --> 00:33:41.470
it's not real but coming from you.

00:33:41.470 --> 00:33:42.578
And by the way,

00:33:42.578 --> 00:33:44.644
we are still in chapter 11;

00:33:44.644 --> 00:33:46.770
trying to see if anything ever started

00:33:46.770 --> 00:33:49.020
or anything ever stopped.

00:33:49.020 --> 00:33:52.540
So, is it artificial?

00:33:52.540 --> 00:33:53.373
Yes.

00:33:53.373 --> 00:33:55.210
Did it happen?

00:33:55.210 --> 00:33:56.120
No.

00:33:56.120 --> 00:33:57.300
Did it happen from you?

00:33:57.300 --> 00:34:00.376
Yes. Got it?

00:34:00.376 --> 00:34:03.048
Alright, let's go to the next one.

00:34:07.720 --> 00:34:09.600
We are now moving to chapter 12,

00:34:09.600 --> 00:34:10.833
which I will remember,

00:34:10.833 --> 00:34:13.674
which as I will remind you,

00:34:13.674 --> 00:34:15.824
was an investigation of

00:34:15.824 --> 00:34:20.206
whether pain was created by pain

00:34:20.206 --> 00:34:22.760
or something else.

00:34:22.760 --> 00:34:24.818
And then the title of

00:34:24.818 --> 00:34:28.550
the chapter can be read differently.

00:34:28.550 --> 00:34:29.800
Was the pain in

00:34:29.800 --> 00:34:31.720
your life created by you

00:34:31.720 --> 00:34:33.050
or by someone else?

00:34:33.050 --> 00:34:37.280
Is the trouble in your life your fault,

00:34:37.280 --> 00:34:38.288
or your husband's fault,

00:34:38.288 --> 00:34:39.121
or your wife's fault?

00:34:39.121 --> 00:34:41.590
Is the trouble in your life

00:34:41.590 --> 00:34:43.510
created by you or by somebody else?

00:34:43.510 --> 00:34:46.460
Or you can say, does pain cause pain

00:34:46.460 --> 00:34:48.400
or does non-pain cause pain?

00:34:48.400 --> 00:34:49.633
There's two ways

00:34:49.633 --> 00:34:52.041
to read the chapter title.

00:34:52.041 --> 00:34:55.619
And we have four possibilities.

00:34:55.619 --> 00:34:57.700
Number one, and by the way,

00:34:57.700 --> 00:34:58.925
these are representing

00:34:58.925 --> 00:35:00.216
four different schools

00:35:00.216 --> 00:35:01.491
of ancient thought, and

00:35:01.491 --> 00:35:03.110
that's how we started this chapter.

00:35:03.110 --> 00:35:04.110
Where does pain come from?

00:35:04.110 --> 00:35:09.110
Number one: was pain caused by itself,

00:35:09.810 --> 00:35:11.810
which is the Sankya position?

00:35:11.810 --> 00:35:14.040
Did God create pain?

00:35:14.040 --> 00:35:16.850
Second position:

00:35:16.850 --> 00:35:17.941
is the pain caused by

00:35:17.941 --> 00:35:20.241
something other than Michael?

00:35:20.241 --> 00:35:21.732
When Michael touches

00:35:21.732 --> 00:35:23.750
a cactus and gets pain,

00:35:23.750 --> 00:35:25.058
did something outside

00:35:25.058 --> 00:35:26.583
of Michael hurt Michael?

00:35:26.583 --> 00:35:28.560
Yeah, you could say that.

00:35:28.560 --> 00:35:30.890
Was it both,

00:35:30.890 --> 00:35:33.070
both God and something else?

00:35:33.070 --> 00:35:34.920
Jains say that.

00:35:34.920 --> 00:35:36.078
There's a religion in

00:35:36.078 --> 00:35:37.780
India that says that.

00:35:37.780 --> 00:35:40.246
And then did it just happen

00:35:40.246 --> 00:35:41.710
and nobody made it happen?

00:35:41.710 --> 00:35:44.420
That's a position by the Charvakas,

00:35:44.420 --> 00:35:46.370
which is a certain school

00:35:46.370 --> 00:35:47.787
of ancient India,

00:35:47.787 --> 00:35:50.813
who don't believe in karma.

00:35:50.813 --> 00:35:54.700
So these are four possibilities.

00:35:54.700 --> 00:35:56.550
We normally say pain is caused

00:35:56.550 --> 00:35:58.524
by something other than me,

00:35:58.524 --> 00:36:00.682
like the cactus caused...

00:36:00.682 --> 00:36:02.890
the cactus hurt my finger.

00:36:02.890 --> 00:36:07.080
Let's go to the next one...

00:36:10.752 --> 00:36:12.235
Now, this is almost the

00:36:12.235 --> 00:36:13.468
only normal argument

00:36:13.468 --> 00:36:15.118
I allowed in this class,

00:36:15.118 --> 00:36:16.784
in this whole course.

00:36:16.784 --> 00:36:19.303
This one is a normal argument.

00:36:19.303 --> 00:36:21.228
If I say to you,

00:36:21.228 --> 00:36:23.340
the pain of this employee

00:36:23.340 --> 00:36:24.798
is being caused by

00:36:24.798 --> 00:36:26.373
someone else or by him?

00:36:26.373 --> 00:36:30.430
What's your answer?

00:36:30.430 --> 00:36:32.140
The employee is in pain.

00:36:32.140 --> 00:36:34.848
If you've ever been an

00:36:34.848 --> 00:36:35.900
employee in a big company,

00:36:35.900 --> 00:36:39.050
you go through this like every day.

00:36:39.050 --> 00:36:41.917
Who caused the trouble for the employee?

00:36:41.917 --> 00:36:44.731
Who's hurting the employee?

00:36:44.731 --> 00:36:46.500
Himself, that's all.

00:36:46.500 --> 00:36:47.675
I tried to put one

00:36:47.675 --> 00:36:49.816
normal thing in the future.

00:36:49.816 --> 00:36:52.216
It looks like the boss

00:36:52.216 --> 00:36:55.200
is hurting the employee.

00:36:55.200 --> 00:36:57.170
There's two famous problems in life.

00:36:57.170 --> 00:36:58.960
One is how your boss treats you

00:36:58.960 --> 00:37:01.390
and one is how your spouse treats you.

00:37:01.390 --> 00:37:03.848
There's just two. Kids are

00:37:03.848 --> 00:37:07.302
probably a subset of spouses.

00:37:07.302 --> 00:37:10.077
And this is so common if you've

00:37:10.077 --> 00:37:11.410
worked in a big company,

00:37:11.410 --> 00:37:12.651
somebody's yelling at you,

00:37:12.651 --> 00:37:13.530
somebody's hurting you.

00:37:13.530 --> 00:37:14.520
Who's hurting?

00:37:14.520 --> 00:37:16.320
Is he being hurt by himself

00:37:16.320 --> 00:37:21.320
or is he being hurt by someone else?

00:37:22.050 --> 00:37:25.100
By himself, he's being hurt by himself.

00:37:25.100 --> 00:37:29.623
That's easy. That was a normal question.

00:37:29.623 --> 00:37:34.235
All right, we're on to chapter 13.

00:37:34.235 --> 00:37:35.701
And chapter 13

00:37:35.701 --> 00:37:38.143
was called an investigation of factors.

00:37:38.143 --> 00:37:40.010
And what should have... the question

00:37:40.010 --> 00:37:42.290
you should have asked yourself was,

00:37:42.290 --> 00:37:44.330
'Why did they teach this chapter

00:37:44.330 --> 00:37:49.330
in addition to..." which chapter?

00:37:49.340 --> 00:37:51.265
Come on, the first chapter,

00:37:51.265 --> 00:37:52.564
the first chapter

00:37:52.564 --> 00:37:53.880
is called an Investigation

00:37:53.880 --> 00:37:56.338
of Conditions,

00:37:56.338 --> 00:37:58.140
Causes and Conditions.

00:37:58.140 --> 00:38:00.430
And now, 13 chapters later,

00:38:00.430 --> 00:38:03.430
they're using the same thing? Factors?

00:38:03.430 --> 00:38:05.400
What's that all about?

00:38:05.400 --> 00:38:07.090
It should have been named...

00:38:07.090 --> 00:38:09.430
This chapter should have been named

00:38:09.430 --> 00:38:11.988
"An Investigation of..."

00:38:11.988 --> 00:38:15.121
this is a clue in the picture...

00:38:15.121 --> 00:38:19.162
- [Student] Real and Unreal.
- Real and Unreal.

00:38:19.162 --> 00:38:21.070
Yeah, fake and real.

00:38:21.070 --> 00:38:24.178
Or an Investigation of Illusion.

00:38:24.178 --> 00:38:25.469
That would be a better

00:38:25.469 --> 00:38:26.744
name for this chapter.

00:38:26.744 --> 00:38:27.693
It's really

00:38:27.693 --> 00:38:30.127
an investigation of illusion.

00:38:30.127 --> 00:38:35.100
Now, got to ask it...

00:38:38.145 --> 00:38:40.380
I'm having trouble with this.

00:38:40.380 --> 00:38:42.080
Let's take that one,

00:38:42.080 --> 00:38:44.090
use that one, use the purse.

00:38:44.090 --> 00:38:45.750
Use the purse.

00:38:45.750 --> 00:38:50.666
Is it real or not?

00:38:51.890 --> 00:38:53.750
Yeah, it's real but it's fake.

00:38:53.750 --> 00:38:55.066
It's real but it's fake.

00:38:55.066 --> 00:38:56.283
No it's fake but it's real.

00:38:56.283 --> 00:38:58.253
I'm sorry.
- [Student] okay.

00:38:58.253 --> 00:38:59.540
- It's fake but it's real.

00:38:59.540 --> 00:39:01.640
What do I mean? It's a fake...

00:39:01.640 --> 00:39:03.350
- [Student] It's an imitation.

00:39:03.350 --> 00:39:05.318
- Yeah, it's a fake Gucci but

00:39:05.318 --> 00:39:07.143
you can still carry

00:39:07.143 --> 00:39:08.434
your wallet around in this.

00:39:08.434 --> 00:39:09.510
Okay. Got it?

00:39:09.510 --> 00:39:14.479
Fake real, no, sorry, a real fake.

00:39:14.479 --> 00:39:16.640
Is it what it looks like?

00:39:16.640 --> 00:39:17.580
No.

00:39:17.580 --> 00:39:18.820
Can it work?

00:39:18.820 --> 00:39:19.653
Yes.

00:39:19.653 --> 00:39:21.570
Is the world what it looks like?

00:39:21.570 --> 00:39:22.403
No.

00:39:22.403 --> 00:39:23.236
Does it work?

00:39:23.236 --> 00:39:24.090
Yes.

00:39:24.090 --> 00:39:25.356
If you don't believe me,

00:39:25.356 --> 00:39:27.100
go stand in front of a car

00:39:27.100 --> 00:39:28.370
and tell me what happens.

00:39:28.370 --> 00:39:32.280
Does the illusory steel in the bumper

00:39:32.280 --> 00:39:36.780
break your illusory leg? Yes.

00:39:36.780 --> 00:39:38.910
We're not saying nothing matters

00:39:38.910 --> 00:39:41.313
and nothing's real.

00:39:48.520 --> 00:39:51.060
The guy, now the other guy says,

00:39:51.060 --> 00:39:54.085
look, do the leaves

00:39:54.085 --> 00:39:56.418
change in the autumn?

00:39:56.418 --> 00:39:59.840
Does the color of the leaves change

00:39:59.840 --> 00:40:01.461
when the autumn comes?

00:40:01.461 --> 00:40:05.700
Do leaves change from green to yellow?

00:40:05.700 --> 00:40:06.533
Yes or no?

00:40:06.533 --> 00:40:07.964
- [Student] Yes.

00:40:07.964 --> 00:40:08.871
- Yes.

00:40:08.871 --> 00:40:12.498
Were they green to start?

00:40:12.498 --> 00:40:13.581
- [Student] Yes.

00:40:13.581 --> 00:40:17.960
- Yes, so did they have an
identity when we started?

00:40:17.960 --> 00:40:20.542
Were they green?

00:40:20.542 --> 00:40:23.571
Are green leaves green?

00:40:23.571 --> 00:40:25.930
Yes, so they have a nature, they're green.

00:40:25.930 --> 00:40:28.880
If they didn't have a nature of green

00:40:28.880 --> 00:40:31.460
how could they change to another color?

00:40:31.460 --> 00:40:33.943
If green was not in them

00:40:33.943 --> 00:40:36.138
how could they become yellow?

00:40:36.138 --> 00:40:37.617
Got it?

00:40:37.617 --> 00:40:39.974
That's a fair question.

00:40:39.974 --> 00:40:42.690
If they weren't green in themselves

00:40:42.690 --> 00:40:47.684
why do you say they turned yellow?

00:40:47.684 --> 00:40:51.367
Now here's the next argument.

00:40:51.367 --> 00:40:53.668
By the way, we say if they were green

00:40:53.668 --> 00:40:56.649
they never would have changed to yellow.

00:40:56.649 --> 00:40:58.040
That's all.

00:40:58.040 --> 00:41:03.011
Your argument proves that you're wrong.

00:41:03.011 --> 00:41:07.795
$100 for this one.

00:41:07.795 --> 00:41:12.150
$100 for this one.

00:41:12.150 --> 00:41:13.550
It's a tough one.

00:41:13.550 --> 00:41:15.008
I'll give you a clue.

00:41:15.008 --> 00:41:16.931
It has to do with emptiness.

00:41:16.931 --> 00:41:21.815
- [Student] (indistinct)

00:41:21.815 --> 00:41:24.641
- Come on. Think about it.

00:41:24.641 --> 00:41:28.770
Did I tell you a joke about
the abbot of the monastery?

00:41:28.770 --> 00:41:30.689
Did I tell you about that story?

00:41:30.689 --> 00:41:35.637
- [Student] What about? (indistinct)

00:41:35.637 --> 00:41:38.650
- No, no, it's a different thing.

00:41:38.650 --> 00:41:40.870
I guess I forgot to tell you this story.

00:41:40.870 --> 00:41:42.570
What's DGAG DBYE?

00:41:42.570 --> 00:41:44.603
- [Student] (indistinct)

00:41:44.603 --> 00:41:46.483
DGAG DBYE is the end
of the summer retreat.

00:41:46.483 --> 00:41:48.397
So for three months in the summer

00:41:48.397 --> 00:41:51.322
all ordained people are supposed to stay

00:41:51.322 --> 00:41:53.345
inside mostly. Why?

00:41:53.345 --> 00:41:55.422
- [Student] So you don't step on bugs.

00:41:55.422 --> 00:41:57.005
So you don't step on bugs.

00:41:57.005 --> 00:41:59.712
So, in India in the summer monosoon,

00:41:59.712 --> 00:42:01.170
and after the monsoon,

00:42:01.170 --> 00:42:02.496
there's millions of bugs around.

00:42:02.496 --> 00:42:03.903
If you step anywhere

00:42:03.903 --> 00:42:05.620
you will kill lots of animals.

00:42:05.620 --> 00:42:09.804
Therefore, in general,
try to stay at home.

00:42:09.804 --> 00:42:12.170
It's like virus, what
you call it?, lockdown.

00:42:12.170 --> 00:42:15.000
In general trying to
stay at home. It's safer.

00:42:15.000 --> 00:42:18.290
Don't go out. If you can
help it, don't go out.

00:42:18.290 --> 00:42:19.640
That's summer retreat.

00:42:19.640 --> 00:42:21.420
DGAG DBYE means

00:42:21.420 --> 00:42:23.345
then you're allowed to come out,

00:42:23.345 --> 00:42:26.070
and it's just like nowadays in Arizona,

00:42:26.070 --> 00:42:28.880
everyone came out.

00:42:28.880 --> 00:42:31.159
Everyone came out, that you can't get

00:42:31.159 --> 00:42:32.988
a restaurant reservation at all

00:42:32.988 --> 00:42:35.760
for this week. Forget it.

00:42:35.760 --> 00:42:40.668
That's why we have to play
our own rock and roll.

00:42:40.668 --> 00:42:44.968
So people come out. And in the monastery,

00:42:44.968 --> 00:42:48.290
you can play games for one week.

00:42:48.290 --> 00:42:51.263
And you can play a radio.
You can play board games.

00:42:51.263 --> 00:42:54.690
You can play soccer. You
can play games on the board.

00:42:54.690 --> 00:42:58.127
You can play carrom,
which is very popular.

00:42:58.127 --> 00:43:00.220
And you can play a radio.

00:43:00.220 --> 00:43:04.313
Now the miracle is, suddenly
everyone has a radio.

00:43:04.313 --> 00:43:06.550
(Students laughing)

00:43:06.550 --> 00:43:09.900
It's truly a miracle.

00:43:09.900 --> 00:43:13.900
SO I remember the joke
I like to tell is...

00:43:13.900 --> 00:43:15.093
I was having a little trouble

00:43:15.093 --> 00:43:16.234
with one of the ex-abbots,

00:43:16.234 --> 00:43:19.124
with an abbot who has
passed away since then.

00:43:19.124 --> 00:43:21.196
We had some disagreements about

00:43:21.196 --> 00:43:24.450
whether all the monks
deserved water or not?

00:43:24.450 --> 00:43:29.433
And I paid for the water
system and I built it.

00:43:29.433 --> 00:43:34.377
So anyway, this is how I
became his best friend.

00:43:34.377 --> 00:43:39.373
I went to his room to have
a discussion with him.

00:43:39.373 --> 00:43:44.368
It was DGAG DBYE. And
here's this very stiff abbot

00:43:44.368 --> 00:43:48.318
sitting on the floor

00:43:48.318 --> 00:43:50.667
sprawled out with his robes everywhere

00:43:50.667 --> 00:43:52.484
and he's playing a board game

00:43:52.484 --> 00:43:55.102
with one of the young monks.

00:43:55.102 --> 00:43:59.632
And I'm like... It came out of my mouth:

00:43:59.632 --> 00:44:02.974
ME LA CHU SHOR NA ...

00:44:02.974 --> 00:44:03.807
Say ME LA

00:44:03.807 --> 00:44:04.648
[Students] ME LA

00:44:04.648 --> 00:44:05.923
Sorry, CHU LA

00:44:05.923 --> 00:44:06.914
[Students] CHU LA

00:44:06.914 --> 00:44:07.747
ME SHOR NA

00:44:07.747 --> 00:44:08.906
[Students] ME SHOR NA

00:44:08.906 --> 00:44:09.739
TE KHA DE

00:44:09.739 --> 00:44:10.572
[Students] TE KHA DE

00:44:10.572 --> 00:44:11.405
CHU LA

00:44:11.405 --> 00:44:12.417
[Students] CHU LA

00:44:12.417 --> 00:44:13.250
ME SHOR NA

00:44:13.250 --> 00:44:14.307
[Students] ME SHO NA

00:44:14.307 --> 00:44:15.140
DE KHA'I

00:44:15.140 --> 00:44:17.165
[Students] TE KHA DE -  What the hell?

00:44:17.165 --> 00:44:18.699
If water catches fire

00:44:18.699 --> 00:44:22.365
what are we going to do?

00:44:22.365 --> 00:44:27.340
How are you going to put
it out? You understand?

00:44:27.340 --> 00:44:31.042
If the guy in charge of making sure

00:44:31.042 --> 00:44:33.710
kids don't play games in the monastery

00:44:33.710 --> 00:44:36.460
is playing a game with one of the kids,

00:44:36.460 --> 00:44:40.635
then who am I going to call to report it?

00:44:40.635 --> 00:44:41.468
It's him.

00:44:41.468 --> 00:44:46.455
That really made me popular with this guy.

00:44:46.455 --> 00:44:50.330
Why am I bringing that up?

00:44:50.330 --> 00:44:51.841
The older you get

00:44:51.841 --> 00:44:56.838
the more strength you have, right?

00:44:56.838 --> 00:44:59.552
I'll give you a clue,
it's about emptiness.

00:44:59.552 --> 00:45:02.940
- [Student](indistinct)

00:45:02.940 --> 00:45:04.465
I better tell you or else

00:45:04.465 --> 00:45:07.623
we'll never finish the class.

00:45:07.623 --> 00:45:10.131
If you're a Buddhist

00:45:10.131 --> 00:45:12.622
and if you're studying emptiness

00:45:12.622 --> 00:45:17.565
and as you study emptiness
you have the instinct

00:45:17.565 --> 00:45:20.440
that emptiness is coming
from its own side,

00:45:20.440 --> 00:45:22.257
you have destroyed the only

00:45:22.257 --> 00:45:24.281
antidote in the world.

00:45:26.687 --> 00:45:28.111
A miseducated Buddhist

00:45:28.111 --> 00:45:31.030
is more dangerous than anybody.

00:45:31.030 --> 00:45:33.021
A wrongly educated Buddhist

00:45:33.021 --> 00:45:35.330
is a truly dangerous thing.

00:45:35.330 --> 00:45:38.235
A Buddhist using mantras
who doesn't understand

00:45:38.235 --> 00:45:41.110
why the mantra works is dangerous.

00:45:41.110 --> 00:45:43.020
Because they go around selling

00:45:43.020 --> 00:45:44.820
something that doesn't work.

00:45:44.820 --> 00:45:46.535
It's like a person who
sells fire extinguishers

00:45:46.535 --> 00:45:47.509
that don't work.

00:45:47.509 --> 00:45:50.300
What could be more cynical

00:45:50.300 --> 00:45:52.058
than to sell fire extinguishers

00:45:52.058 --> 00:45:55.087
that you know they don't work?

00:45:55.087 --> 00:45:58.570
What could be more cruel

00:45:58.570 --> 00:46:00.790
than to go sell 100 fire extinguishers

00:46:00.790 --> 00:46:02.948
then the place catches on fire

00:46:02.948 --> 00:46:04.281
and it doesn't work.

00:46:06.305 --> 00:46:08.362
In a way, we must educate ourselves

00:46:08.362 --> 00:46:10.109
about what emptiness really is.

00:46:10.109 --> 00:46:14.660
Because if you come to
misunderstand emptiness

00:46:14.660 --> 00:46:16.409
it will never work for you

00:46:16.409 --> 00:46:18.717
and then you'll always suffer. Got it?

00:46:18.717 --> 00:46:23.448
And same with mantras.

00:46:23.448 --> 00:46:25.239
If the water catches fire,

00:46:25.239 --> 00:46:27.837
if the emptiness is self-exi...,

00:46:27.837 --> 00:46:30.348
if you think the emptiness
is self-existent,

00:46:30.348 --> 00:46:31.878
then we have a problem.

00:46:31.878 --> 00:46:36.878
Then we can't fix anything. Got it?

00:46:40.253 --> 00:46:42.478
I don't know if you remember this one?

00:46:42.478 --> 00:46:44.036
I don't remember if I
really nailed it down.

00:46:44.036 --> 00:46:45.862
I think some of the pictures we skipped.

00:46:45.862 --> 00:46:50.862
Right Pachi? I'm sorry.

00:46:51.904 --> 00:46:53.308
We are in the chapter...

00:46:53.308 --> 00:46:56.417
We're in a new chapter 14 about sansarga.

00:46:56.417 --> 00:47:00.159
My Sanskrit expertise
went to the bathroom.

00:47:00.159 --> 00:47:02.166
What's "sansarga"?

00:47:02.166 --> 00:47:04.990
It means contact, contact between things.

00:47:04.990 --> 00:47:07.260
How do things touch each other?

00:47:07.260 --> 00:47:10.400
It feels correctly like a lot of Nagarjuna

00:47:10.400 --> 00:47:12.383
depends on this question.

00:47:12.383 --> 00:47:17.036
Can anything touch another thing?

00:47:22.022 --> 00:47:23.180
I'll tell you what Nagarjuna

00:47:23.180 --> 00:47:26.066
would say about this picture.

00:47:26.066 --> 00:47:27.566
If you want money bad

00:47:27.566 --> 00:47:29.585
enough to hurt someone to get it,

00:47:29.585 --> 00:47:31.998
you cannot touch the money.

00:47:31.998 --> 00:47:36.530
If you want money bad enough
to compete with someone else

00:47:36.530 --> 00:47:40.036
to get the money, then
you will never touch...

00:47:40.036 --> 00:47:43.317
The money cannot touch your hand.

00:47:43.317 --> 00:47:45.800
Does that mean you can't hold money?

00:47:45.800 --> 00:47:48.208
No, it just means the money is unreal.

00:47:48.208 --> 00:47:51.007
Why?

00:47:51.007 --> 00:47:53.150
It looks like you got it by taking it

00:47:53.150 --> 00:47:55.950
but you didn't. You got
it by being generous.

00:47:55.950 --> 00:47:57.291
You got it by making

00:47:57.291 --> 00:47:59.791
a donation to Club de Oro last week.

00:47:59.791 --> 00:48:03.141
And the money you think you stole

00:48:03.141 --> 00:48:06.615
isn't the money you stole.

00:48:06.615 --> 00:48:08.066
This is the money you got

00:48:08.066 --> 00:48:10.170
because you donated last week. Got it?

00:48:10.170 --> 00:48:14.894
She doesn't have any money in her hands.

00:48:14.894 --> 00:48:16.715
Because she thinks it came from stealing.

00:48:16.715 --> 00:48:20.532
But it didn't, it can't.

00:48:20.532 --> 00:48:22.066
Next one.

00:48:29.325 --> 00:48:31.500
What was this lesson,
do you guys remember?

00:48:31.500 --> 00:48:32.333
- [Student] Short and tall.

00:48:32.333 --> 00:48:34.824
- Yes, but with what context?

00:48:34.824 --> 00:48:38.465
- [Student] Can you have
shortness without tallness?

00:48:38.465 --> 00:48:41.515
- Yes, can you recognize...

00:48:41.515 --> 00:48:42.348
What?

00:48:42.348 --> 00:48:44.707
- [Student] Could you
recognize shortness...

00:48:44.707 --> 00:48:47.077
- Yes, without a tall person.

00:48:47.077 --> 00:48:49.235
And the Buddhist answer is?

00:48:49.235 --> 00:48:51.060
- [Student] Yes.

00:48:51.060 --> 00:48:53.500
- Yes, because it's coming from your mind.

00:48:53.500 --> 00:48:58.420
- I've heard the weird explanations

00:48:58.420 --> 00:49:01.470
by American untrained Buddhists who say,

00:49:01.470 --> 00:49:04.046
oh Buddhism is all about...

00:49:04.046 --> 00:49:06.611
In fact somebody wrote a book about it.

00:49:06.611 --> 00:49:10.185
Buddhism is all about comparison,

00:49:10.185 --> 00:49:11.384
what do you call it?

00:49:11.384 --> 00:49:14.190
Short you can't see...

00:49:14.190 --> 00:49:16.123
Short comes from long.

00:49:16.123 --> 00:49:17.364
Basically it was saying that,

00:49:17.364 --> 00:49:20.875
everything is... Dependence...
Dependent origination

00:49:20.875 --> 00:49:22.300
means you can't recognize short

00:49:22.300 --> 00:49:25.707
until you have long. And
that's completely false,

00:49:25.707 --> 00:49:28.280
since Buddha never said
anything like that.

00:49:28.280 --> 00:49:31.050
In fact the Buddha would say the opposite.

00:49:31.050 --> 00:49:32.610
Which is what?

00:49:32.610 --> 00:49:34.860
You can think something is long

00:49:34.860 --> 00:49:37.163
without something which is short

00:49:37.163 --> 00:49:39.710
because it's coming from
your mind, that's all.

00:49:39.710 --> 00:49:42.143
It doesn't depend on two outside objects,

00:49:42.143 --> 00:49:43.543
comparing them.

00:49:43.543 --> 00:49:45.780
That's not where a short comes from.

00:49:45.780 --> 00:49:46.901
Short comes from your mind.

00:49:46.901 --> 00:49:47.734
You can have lots of shorts

00:49:47.734 --> 00:49:49.409
without talls,

00:49:49.409 --> 00:49:50.242
all over.

00:49:53.917 --> 00:49:55.360
You can find those books,

00:49:55.360 --> 00:49:58.558
it's amazing.

00:50:01.900 --> 00:50:02.733
Next one.

00:50:03.858 --> 00:50:05.765
I don't know if you remember

00:50:05.765 --> 00:50:09.433
but let's go back to the easiest example.

00:50:09.433 --> 00:50:11.075
There's a part of the path

00:50:11.075 --> 00:50:12.845
that you walked on already,

00:50:12.845 --> 00:50:14.444
there's a part of the path

00:50:14.444 --> 00:50:15.811
that you didn't reach yet

00:50:15.811 --> 00:50:18.550
and there's a part of the path between.

00:50:18.550 --> 00:50:20.240
Does the part of the path...

00:50:20.240 --> 00:50:22.583
By the way this chapter is about sansarga

00:50:22.583 --> 00:50:25.333
which means contact.

00:50:25.333 --> 00:50:26.174
Can the part of the path

00:50:26.174 --> 00:50:29.040
that you already walked
on ever make contact

00:50:29.040 --> 00:50:30.081
with the part of the path

00:50:30.081 --> 00:50:32.681
that you're going to walk on?

00:50:32.681 --> 00:50:34.148
- [Student] Yes.

00:50:34.148 --> 00:50:36.723
- Cannot.

00:50:36.723 --> 00:50:39.550
Unless you don't look so close.

00:50:39.550 --> 00:50:41.582
And that's a Buddhist principle.

00:50:41.582 --> 00:50:43.506
Unless you don't look so close.

00:50:43.506 --> 00:50:47.592
MA BRTAG MA DPYAD PA

00:50:47.592 --> 00:50:50.330
without investigation, without checking.

00:50:50.330 --> 00:50:53.830
I mean, if you're worried...

00:50:53.830 --> 00:50:55.547
If you're trying to drive back

00:50:55.547 --> 00:50:57.037
to Rimrock this afternoon

00:50:57.037 --> 00:51:00.268
to get your nap on time,

00:51:00.268 --> 00:51:01.989
and you sit there and worry about

00:51:01.989 --> 00:51:03.674
which part of the road
did you already drive on,

00:51:03.674 --> 00:51:05.371
which part of the road
you didn't drive on,

00:51:05.371 --> 00:51:07.121
you're going to get in a car accident,

00:51:07.121 --> 00:51:08.713
you're never going to get home.

00:51:08.713 --> 00:51:11.614
There are appropriate times in our life

00:51:11.614 --> 00:51:14.725
when you should just god-damn drive home

00:51:14.725 --> 00:51:17.372
and don't worry about where you are.

00:51:17.372 --> 00:51:19.251
You're going to get a car accident.

00:51:19.251 --> 00:51:23.658
So it's called MA BRTAG MA DPYAD PA

00:51:23.658 --> 00:51:25.994
Does the part of the road to the Rimrock

00:51:25.994 --> 00:51:28.903
that I already drove on ever touched...

00:51:28.903 --> 00:51:32.402
- did they ever intersect?
That's the point -

00:51:32.402 --> 00:51:33.727
...ever touched the part of road

00:51:33.727 --> 00:51:35.001
I haven't driven on yet7

00:51:35.001 --> 00:51:37.357
Look, there's times in life

00:51:37.357 --> 00:51:39.598
when you don't want to worry about it.

00:51:39.598 --> 00:51:42.817
Just don't hit the traffic
in the Easter Holiday

00:51:42.817 --> 00:51:44.658
and don't crash into anybody.

00:51:44.658 --> 00:51:46.975
When you get home, before your nap

00:51:46.975 --> 00:51:48.099
you can think about it.

00:51:48.099 --> 00:51:50.978
MA BRTAG MA DPYAD PA
means, do they intersect?

00:51:50.978 --> 00:51:53.420
Yes, if you don't look at it too closely.

00:51:53.420 --> 00:51:55.507
If you don't look at it too closely.

00:51:55.507 --> 00:51:59.186
Very famous Buddhist principle.

00:51:59.186 --> 00:52:02.070
- Should I do my mantra,
or shouldn't do mantras?

00:52:02.070 --> 00:52:03.870
- Look, relax and do your mantras.

00:52:03.870 --> 00:52:05.253
- But they don't work!

00:52:05.253 --> 00:52:06.827
- I know they don't work,

00:52:06.827 --> 00:52:08.088
but they're going to work.

00:52:08.088 --> 00:52:08.946
Just be nice to people,

00:52:08.946 --> 00:52:10.479
and your mantra is going to work.

00:52:10.479 --> 00:52:13.351
- Ah, okay good, I don't
have to stop my mantras.

00:52:13.351 --> 00:52:15.641
Geshe-la never said, "don't do mantras."

00:52:15.641 --> 00:52:19.200
Geshe-la said, "do mantras with wisdom

00:52:19.200 --> 00:52:20.780
and then they work."

00:52:20.780 --> 00:52:22.551
- But if I don't have wisdom

00:52:22.551 --> 00:52:23.467
can I still do my mantras?

00:52:23.467 --> 00:52:24.300
- Yes.

00:52:24.300 --> 00:52:25.370
- Will it help me?

00:52:25.370 --> 00:52:27.960
- Yes, your intention is very powerful.

00:52:27.960 --> 00:52:32.140
Go ahead, but later try to study,

00:52:32.140 --> 00:52:35.762
why they work, which is this book.

00:52:35.762 --> 00:52:38.405
By the way this is the most famous book

00:52:38.405 --> 00:52:40.030
about why mantras work.

00:52:40.030 --> 00:52:45.030
In fact the author was

00:52:45.063 --> 00:52:46.804
the highest

00:52:46.804 --> 00:52:49.139
tantrika an Indian history!

00:52:49.139 --> 00:52:52.820
Duh! Maybe there's a connection.

00:52:54.003 --> 00:52:56.153
Eight thousand pages of books

00:52:56.153 --> 00:52:57.820
about his ideas of tantra,

00:52:57.820 --> 00:53:01.500
maybe he knew what he was talking about.

00:53:04.158 --> 00:53:05.187
What's the next picture?

00:53:05.187 --> 00:53:07.153
Tell me a story somebody.

00:53:07.153 --> 00:53:09.400
- [Student] The real cream or...

00:53:09.400 --> 00:53:12.150
- Yes, now tell me this story, come on,

00:53:12.150 --> 00:53:15.726
don't make me repeat the story.

00:53:15.726 --> 00:53:17.792
- [Student] Geshe-la
used to drive his lama.

00:53:17.792 --> 00:53:20.870
- Yes, Geshe-la used to drive his lama.

00:53:20.870 --> 00:53:23.385
For 20 years, every month.

00:53:23.385 --> 00:53:25.140
- [Student] Five hundred times.

00:53:25.140 --> 00:53:25.973
- Yes.

00:53:25.973 --> 00:53:26.806
- [Student] Once thee stopped...

00:53:26.806 --> 00:53:28.439
- Yes, we stopped at Howard Johnson

00:53:28.439 --> 00:53:30.255
next to Delaware Bridge,

00:53:30.255 --> 00:53:33.990
probably, were going to have
to put a plaque there now.

00:53:33.990 --> 00:53:36.480
And Rinpoche would say, "Tell the lady

00:53:36.480 --> 00:53:41.480
I don't want that artificial cream."

00:53:41.764 --> 00:53:45.727
Meaning if it's created it's not natural.

00:53:45.727 --> 00:53:48.227
We are creating the world.

00:53:48.227 --> 00:53:51.043
It's very similar to powdered cream

00:53:51.043 --> 00:53:52.210
as opposed to real cream.

00:53:52.210 --> 00:53:54.748
Does it work? Well, that's a question.

00:53:54.748 --> 00:53:55.920
(chuckling)

00:53:55.920 --> 00:53:58.975
Next picture...

00:53:58.975 --> 00:54:01.216
By the way we've moved on to chapter 15

00:54:01.216 --> 00:54:05.230
which is called "An
Investigation of RANG BZHIN."

00:54:05.230 --> 00:54:06.754
For a hundred bucks, Tim,

00:54:06.754 --> 00:54:08.362
give me a nice translation

00:54:08.362 --> 00:54:10.493
for RANG BZHIN in this case.

00:54:12.490 --> 00:54:15.857
Which means it's not the
one you normally knew.

00:54:15.857 --> 00:54:19.250
It's not... Oh, I almost said it for you.

00:54:19.250 --> 00:54:20.940
It's not nature here.

00:54:20.940 --> 00:54:23.756
I mean there's a better
word you could use.

00:54:23.756 --> 00:54:25.780
- [Tim] (indistinct)

00:54:25.780 --> 00:54:28.400
Well, what  in the selisf-existent nature?

00:54:28.400 --> 00:54:30.200
Give me the word.

00:54:30.200 --> 00:54:31.210
We found a better word

00:54:31.210 --> 00:54:35.227
in fact I'm going to
change my translation.

00:54:35.227 --> 00:54:36.514
- [Tim](indistinct)

00:54:36.514 --> 00:54:39.450
- Anyway, identity.

00:54:39.450 --> 00:54:41.720
Do things have an identity?

00:54:41.720 --> 00:54:44.480
Do they have a natural identity?

00:54:44.480 --> 00:54:47.810
And the first example we have is...

00:54:47.810 --> 00:54:51.070
Somebody, explain the example to me.

00:54:51.070 --> 00:54:52.355
Is this the last picture, by the way?

00:54:52.355 --> 00:54:55.318
No, we still have some more.

00:54:55.318 --> 00:54:57.323
What's happening here?

00:54:57.323 --> 00:54:59.048
- [Student] Two husbands.

00:54:59.048 --> 00:55:01.500
- Two ways to fall off. In the kitchen

00:55:01.500 --> 00:55:03.360
when you're having your
argument with your husband

00:55:03.360 --> 00:55:05.000
there's two extremes you can fall off.

00:55:05.000 --> 00:55:07.742
First one...

00:55:07.742 --> 00:55:11.533
which is the one that everyone falls off.

00:55:13.130 --> 00:55:14.882
What's the most common misunderstanding

00:55:14.882 --> 00:55:16.627
when you're having an
argument with your husband?

00:55:16.627 --> 00:55:17.460
- [Students](indistinct)

00:55:17.460 --> 00:55:19.250
- It's not coming from me.

00:55:19.250 --> 00:55:21.610
I don't know what's wrong with him today.

00:55:21.610 --> 00:55:24.185
He's hungry, he had a bad day,

00:55:24.185 --> 00:55:25.625
there was a lot of traffic.

00:55:25.625 --> 00:55:26.830
We make up all these reasons

00:55:26.830 --> 00:55:29.360
why he's being mean to you.

00:55:29.360 --> 00:55:32.990
That's one extreme.

00:55:32.990 --> 00:55:34.633
He's coming from his own side.

00:55:35.730 --> 00:55:40.730
Now the second extreme is only fallen into

00:55:41.329 --> 00:55:44.397
by badly trained Buddhists.

00:55:44.397 --> 00:55:45.680
- [Student](indistinct)

00:55:45.680 --> 00:55:49.240
- Yes, if he's not coming from his side,

00:55:49.240 --> 00:55:51.180
you always have to say "if",

00:55:51.180 --> 00:55:54.570
if he's not coming from his side, then

00:55:54.570 --> 00:55:57.280
he don't exist: maya, illusion,

00:55:57.280 --> 00:56:00.740
he's not there at all.

00:56:00.740 --> 00:56:02.389
If the mantra doesn't exist

00:56:02.389 --> 00:56:04.865
the way I thought it existed,

00:56:04.865 --> 00:56:08.220
there is no mantra.

00:56:08.220 --> 00:56:09.803
If the mantra doesn't work

00:56:09.803 --> 00:56:11.220
the way I thought it did

00:56:11.220 --> 00:56:13.040
there is no mantra.

00:56:13.040 --> 00:56:16.510
That you fell off of
both edges of the bridge.

00:56:16.510 --> 00:56:19.819
What's the proper
attitude about the mantra?

00:56:19.819 --> 00:56:22.277
It does work but only...

00:56:24.100 --> 00:56:24.933
- [Student] if I loaded it

00:56:24.933 --> 00:56:26.530
- ..,try to protect life,

00:56:26.530 --> 00:56:28.032
if I try to protect life.

00:56:28.032 --> 00:56:32.042
Yes, if I loaded it like a stapler.

00:56:32.042 --> 00:56:32.900
Nice answers.

00:56:32.900 --> 00:56:34.716
Let's go, we're almost done.

00:56:34.716 --> 00:56:36.199
Hang in here.

00:56:37.420 --> 00:56:39.050
The next chapter is 16.

00:56:39.050 --> 00:56:41.441
By the way, we only get to 17

00:56:41.441 --> 00:56:42.970
and we're done. Yཨy!

00:56:42.970 --> 00:56:46.270
That's called "An Investigation of Bondage

00:56:46.270 --> 00:56:48.650
and Freedom from Bondage."

00:56:48.650 --> 00:56:52.130
Chained up and breaking the chains.

00:56:52.130 --> 00:56:56.730
Like Schwarzenegger.

00:56:56.730 --> 00:57:00.255
And this picture was called

00:57:00.255 --> 00:57:03.138
removing the handcuffs from a nobody

00:57:03.138 --> 00:57:05.121
and it means,

00:57:07.762 --> 00:57:11.469
who is chained to what?

00:57:11.469 --> 00:57:14.419
I'm chained to or ...

00:57:14.419 --> 00:57:17.270
Yes, good, or my body and mind.

00:57:17.270 --> 00:57:19.780
I'm chained to a mortal body.

00:57:19.780 --> 00:57:22.070
As you get older it becomes serious.

00:57:22.070 --> 00:57:24.560
When you're younger, it's okay.

00:57:24.560 --> 00:57:25.393
But when you're later

00:57:25.393 --> 00:57:28.510
you're like... the body's falling apart

00:57:28.510 --> 00:57:30.170
and then you realize you're chained to it,

00:57:30.170 --> 00:57:32.190
you cannot get away from it.

00:57:32.190 --> 00:57:36.240
And your mind is also,
you chained to your mind,

00:57:36.240 --> 00:57:39.123
and neither one is healthy.

00:57:39.123 --> 00:57:40.439
They are falling apart,

00:57:40.439 --> 00:57:41.272
and you can't get away,

00:57:41.272 --> 00:57:43.735
your chained to it.

00:57:43.735 --> 00:57:45.660
Then Nagarjuna says,

00:57:45.660 --> 00:57:47.918
"No, the thing you think

00:57:47.918 --> 00:57:51.000
you're chained to is not real."

00:57:51.000 --> 00:57:53.770
You are chained to something you produce.

00:57:53.770 --> 00:57:55.511
You are chained to something

00:57:55.511 --> 00:57:57.340
you are seeing get old

00:57:57.340 --> 00:57:59.580
because you didn't take
care of your seeds.

00:57:59.580 --> 00:58:00.907
So just take care of your seeds,

00:58:00.907 --> 00:58:05.907
and you won't be chained anymore.

00:58:06.060 --> 00:58:09.060
That's freedom from bondage.

00:58:09.060 --> 00:58:10.463
Next one, you guys.

00:58:14.670 --> 00:58:16.361
This is chapter 17.

00:58:16.361 --> 00:58:17.752
We reached the last chapter.

00:58:17.752 --> 00:58:21.389
The chapter of the investigation of?

00:58:21.389 --> 00:58:22.430
- [Student] Karma.

00:58:22.430 --> 00:58:23.880
- Karma.

00:58:23.880 --> 00:58:25.870
Which is a long chapter.

00:58:25.870 --> 00:58:28.212
We spent a couple of classes on it,

00:58:28.212 --> 00:58:31.553
two or three classes.

00:58:31.553 --> 00:58:36.503
This represents "chetana"
and "chetayitva".

00:58:37.580 --> 00:58:40.475
Yes, karma in the form of?

00:58:40.475 --> 00:58:41.550
- [Student] Karma in form of intention.

00:58:41.550 --> 00:58:44.320
-Yes, karma in the form of intention

00:58:44.320 --> 00:58:45.803
and then what you did.

00:58:45.803 --> 00:58:49.060
Either good or bad intention.

00:58:49.060 --> 00:58:51.385
When Buddha taught karma,
it's interesting...

00:58:51.385 --> 00:58:52.868
I think

00:58:52.868 --> 00:58:56.837
that Nagarjuna first talks about karma

00:58:56.837 --> 00:58:58.620
in the context of thinking

00:58:58.620 --> 00:59:01.086
and doing what you thought to do.

00:59:01.086 --> 00:59:02.888
He doesn't say ten kinds of deeds

00:59:02.888 --> 00:59:04.290
or something like that.

00:59:04.290 --> 00:59:07.790
He says, "All karma is divided into

00:59:07.790 --> 00:59:12.780
what you're thinking and
what you thought to do."

00:59:12.780 --> 00:59:14.790
Which is very... what's school?

00:59:14.790 --> 00:59:17.706
,,LAS LAS 'JIG RTEN SNA TSOGS
SKYES, ,DE NI SEMS PA DANG DES BYAS,

00:59:17.706 --> 00:59:18.539
- [Student] Abhidharma.

00:59:18.539 --> 00:59:19.373
- Abhidharma.

00:59:19.373 --> 00:59:23.436
Why is he so fixed on Abhidharma?

00:59:23.436 --> 00:59:26.859
The other schools didn't exist yet.

00:59:30.846 --> 00:59:32.667
No Mind-Only school yet.

00:59:32.667 --> 00:59:33.950
No Sautrantika school yet.

00:59:33.950 --> 00:59:37.238
He's early, this stuff is old.

00:59:37.238 --> 00:59:38.980
This stuff is 2000 years old.

00:59:38.980 --> 00:59:40.910
The fact that you can read it,

00:59:40.910 --> 00:59:42.610
a hundred generations later,

00:59:42.610 --> 00:59:44.330
that's something.

00:59:44.330 --> 00:59:46.870
That says something about the lineage.

00:59:46.870 --> 00:59:48.886
The lineage has been kept,

00:59:48.886 --> 00:59:51.460
and it's very beautiful.

00:59:51.460 --> 00:59:55.930
You normally you can't
even talk to your parents.

00:59:55.930 --> 00:59:58.330
No, I mean multiplying
that times a hundred.

00:59:58.330 --> 01:00:01.380
It's a miracle that we
can read this thing.

01:00:01.380 --> 01:00:05.405
It really says something
about the lineage.

01:00:05.405 --> 01:00:10.405
It says something about

01:00:10.462 --> 01:00:12.420
the function of the lineage:

01:00:12.420 --> 01:00:17.420
it kept it for 2000
years, it's unbelievable.

01:00:17.435 --> 01:00:20.432
Two kinds of karma: thinking

01:00:20.432 --> 01:00:22.690
and what the thinking inspires you to do.

01:00:22.690 --> 01:00:23.523
Next one.

01:00:25.948 --> 01:00:27.707
$100 -- somebody tell me

01:00:27.707 --> 01:00:29.517
why this is relevant?

01:00:29.517 --> 01:00:30.842
$100 dollars...

01:00:30.842 --> 01:00:31.867
God, I'm giving away so much money

01:00:31.867 --> 01:00:33.956
you guys aren't excited,
you're still like...

01:00:33.956 --> 01:00:37.201
(snoring)

01:00:37.201 --> 01:00:42.120
- [Student] ...the same
person walked in...

01:00:44.395 --> 01:00:45.911
- Say it again?

01:00:45.911 --> 01:00:47.903
- [Student] (unclear)

01:00:47.903 --> 01:00:50.076
- That's a good guess but it's wrong.

01:00:53.500 --> 01:00:56.820
What theme was happening in this chapter

01:00:56.820 --> 01:01:01.760
that might be shown in this picture?

01:01:01.760 --> 01:01:03.130
What is this picture?

01:01:03.130 --> 01:01:04.740
What's happening?

01:01:04.740 --> 01:01:06.700
It's a waiting room.

01:01:06.700 --> 01:01:08.413
- [Student] Yes.

01:01:08.413 --> 01:01:09.400
- [Student] Waiting
until the karma ripens.

01:01:09.400 --> 01:01:12.700
Yes good, $100 for the young man.

01:01:12.700 --> 01:01:14.950
You're getting a lot of money today.

01:01:14.950 --> 01:01:17.097
Yes, where is the karma staying

01:01:17.097 --> 01:01:19.413
until it ripens?

01:01:19.413 --> 01:01:24.198
To earn the $100 now:

01:01:26.144 --> 01:01:27.802
if the karma was...

01:01:27.802 --> 01:01:30.265
There's two problems. If it was...

01:01:30.265 --> 01:01:31.860
- [Student] If it was unchanging.

01:01:31.860 --> 01:01:35.668
- If it was unchanging.

01:01:36.577 --> 01:01:39.993
- [Student] If it was unchanging,

01:01:39.993 --> 01:01:42.062
[Student] it wouldn't
be able to produce...

01:01:42.062 --> 01:01:43.629
- Yes, it couldn't produce anything.

01:01:43.629 --> 01:01:45.579
And if it was changing, if

01:01:45.579 --> 01:01:49.190
(snapping fingers)

01:01:49.190 --> 01:01:51.081
...if it was going

01:01:51.081 --> 01:01:53.823
in and out of existence,

01:01:53.823 --> 01:01:57.540
then how can it sustain...
how can it ripen?

01:01:59.324 --> 01:02:04.324
How does karma wait until it opens?

01:02:04.507 --> 01:02:07.960
That's a big issue.

01:02:07.960 --> 01:02:12.745
And this helps to answer
that question, for $100.

01:02:13.790 --> 01:02:17.623
The next picture helps
to answer the question.

01:02:21.744 --> 01:02:23.607
CHUD MI ZA BA

01:02:23.607 --> 01:02:25.380
$100, what's that mean?

01:02:25.380 --> 01:02:27.420
- [Student] It says contract there.

01:02:27.420 --> 01:02:29.254
- Yes, but what does that mean?

01:02:29.254 --> 01:02:31.671
- [Student] It means..(indistinct)

01:02:34.125 --> 01:02:35.760
(laughing)

01:02:35.760 --> 01:02:38.479
- Work it out and then
you can share the money.

01:02:38.479 --> 01:02:39.730
(laughing)

01:02:39.730 --> 01:02:42.060
You have to have a CHUD MI ZA BA.

01:02:42.060 --> 01:02:43.340
You have to have this contract.

01:02:43.340 --> 01:02:46.030
What's the contract say?

01:02:47.770 --> 01:02:50.930
Don't go away or something.

01:02:50.930 --> 01:02:54.590
A don't go away.

01:02:54.590 --> 01:02:56.623
A doesn't go away.

01:02:56.623 --> 01:02:59.260
What doesn't go away?

01:02:59.260 --> 01:03:01.330
The karma, it stays with
you until it ripens,

01:03:01.330 --> 01:03:02.247
until it opens.

01:03:02.247 --> 01:03:03.780
There's a contractual agreement

01:03:03.780 --> 01:03:05.620
between you and your karma.

01:03:05.620 --> 01:03:10.066
As soon as you do how many things?

01:03:10.066 --> 01:03:13.760
Anything. As soon as you do anything

01:03:13.760 --> 01:03:17.760
you get a corresponding 'don't go away.'

01:03:17.760 --> 01:03:19.720
I forget what we call it.

01:03:19.720 --> 01:03:20.600
As soon as you do...

01:03:20.600 --> 01:03:21.900
As soon as you pick your nose,

01:03:21.900 --> 01:03:24.392
you just made like ten don't go aways.

01:03:24.392 --> 01:03:27.317
(laughing)

01:03:27.317 --> 01:03:29.567
And they stay with you,

01:03:29.567 --> 01:03:33.290
and they help explain why the karma,

01:03:33.290 --> 01:03:34.933
whether it changes or it doesn't change,

01:03:34.933 --> 01:03:37.093
it stays with you, because there's glue.

01:03:37.093 --> 01:03:39.575
It's a glue. It's a contractual agreement

01:03:39.575 --> 01:03:41.120
between you and your karmic seeds.

01:03:41.120 --> 01:03:43.278
- You stick with me until you open, okay?

01:03:43.278 --> 01:03:44.597
- Yes, okay...

01:03:44.597 --> 01:03:45.430
- Let's write a contract.

01:03:45.430 --> 01:03:47.177
- Okay.

01:03:47.177 --> 01:03:49.900
You write a contract with your karmas

01:03:49.900 --> 01:03:51.640
and they stick with you till they open.

01:03:53.657 --> 01:03:56.870
Next picture.

01:04:00.790 --> 01:04:04.570
Something rotten is
making something rotten.

01:04:04.570 --> 01:04:07.037
It had to do with the first Arya truth

01:04:09.180 --> 01:04:10.430
and the second Arya truth.

01:04:10.430 --> 01:04:13.900
Second Arya truth has two parts.

01:04:13.900 --> 01:04:15.490
First Arya truth is truth of suffering.

01:04:15.490 --> 01:04:17.406
The money's going down, down, down.

01:04:17.406 --> 01:04:21.398
(laughing)

01:04:23.520 --> 01:04:25.978
There is two parts... karma and?

01:04:25.978 --> 01:04:30.781
- [Student] No, sorry,
karma and negative emotions

01:04:30.781 --> 01:04:35.756
- Yes, karma and negative emotions.

01:04:36.767 --> 01:04:40.980
If the cause is crappy,
then the result is crappy.

01:04:40.980 --> 01:04:43.510
If the apple is rotten then the apple pie

01:04:43.510 --> 01:04:46.050
that you make from it
is going to taste bad.

01:04:46.050 --> 01:04:47.360
What's that mean?

01:04:47.360 --> 01:04:52.347
If the karma and the
negative emotions are impure,

01:04:54.610 --> 01:04:57.326
meaning...

01:04:57.326 --> 01:04:58.168
Good! Self-existent.

01:04:58.168 --> 01:05:00.770
How could they make a? ..

01:05:00.770 --> 01:05:05.290
Yes, how could they make a "pure" result?

01:05:05.290 --> 01:05:07.730
How could you get...

01:05:07.730 --> 01:05:10.020
How could you get a changing result

01:05:10.020 --> 01:05:15.020
from an unchanging action?

01:05:15.830 --> 01:05:19.622
If the action was not empty

01:05:19.622 --> 01:05:20.600
then the action would be...

01:05:20.600 --> 01:05:23.432
If the action had an identity

01:05:23.432 --> 01:05:24.780
then it couldn't change.

01:05:24.780 --> 01:05:27.260
And if it's still made a result,

01:05:27.260 --> 01:05:28.460
life would be weird.

01:05:28.460 --> 01:05:30.660
Then you'd have to be really super careful

01:05:30.660 --> 01:05:32.993
because...

01:05:32.993 --> 01:05:36.410
results would pop up
without doing anything.

01:05:36.410 --> 01:05:38.610
And even in the normal
world they will complain

01:05:38.610 --> 01:05:40.893
if you get...

01:05:40.893 --> 01:05:42.351
- [Student] Watermelon.

01:05:42.351 --> 01:05:46.040
- Watermelon. No, lettuce
growing all over the yard

01:05:46.040 --> 01:05:48.520
which you didn't plant.
Even in the normal world

01:05:48.520 --> 01:05:52.740
people say something's weird. Got it?

01:05:52.740 --> 01:05:56.323
I think we have one
more picture remaining.

01:05:59.647 --> 01:06:02.569
No, is that the last picture?

01:06:02.569 --> 01:06:07.360
Okay, didn't we do the last thing?

01:06:07.360 --> 01:06:08.590
Oh, we didn't do the movie picture?

01:06:08.590 --> 01:06:10.120
Let's do it I'll explain it and

01:06:10.120 --> 01:06:13.770
we'll call it a day.

01:06:18.296 --> 01:06:20.063
You can make some money here.

01:06:20.063 --> 01:06:23.705
$300, last thing, last part of the course.

01:06:23.705 --> 01:06:25.030
Then we're are free.

01:06:25.030 --> 01:06:27.600
Then grandpa can go home and take a nap

01:06:27.600 --> 01:06:29.163
or have 20 meetings.

01:06:32.220 --> 01:06:34.570
For three hundred dollars...

01:06:34.570 --> 01:06:37.150
I'll tell you what the picture was about.

01:06:37.150 --> 01:06:40.383
The picture was about...

01:06:40.383 --> 01:06:43.466
Do you realize this picture was...

01:06:43.466 --> 01:06:47.110
What do you call it?

01:06:47.110 --> 01:06:52.110
...scripted. The picture's not real.

01:06:54.170 --> 01:06:56.230
Somebody paid somebody to
come and stand there so

01:06:56.230 --> 01:07:01.010
they could take a picture
of them making a movie.

01:07:01.010 --> 01:07:05.268
So, it's all fake.

01:07:05.268 --> 01:07:06.893
This picture is fake.

01:07:06.893 --> 01:07:08.484
Somebody paid somebody

01:07:08.484 --> 01:07:10.142
to pretend they were making a movie

01:07:10.142 --> 01:07:15.142
and the movie is also pretending. Got it?

01:07:15.532 --> 01:07:17.373
Isn't it a clever picture?

01:07:17.373 --> 01:07:19.330
Come on, give me some credit.

01:07:19.330 --> 01:07:21.840
Now listen, this is not a picture

01:07:21.840 --> 01:07:24.870
of people making a movie. It's all fake.

01:07:24.870 --> 01:07:27.040
It's somebody paid them
to come and stand there,

01:07:27.040 --> 01:07:28.104
they took a picture,

01:07:28.104 --> 01:07:30.323
they charged me $5 for this picture.

01:07:30.323 --> 01:07:32.300
Because it's fake.

01:07:32.300 --> 01:07:35.300
It's a fake picture of somebody making a

01:07:35.300 --> 01:07:36.150
fake picture.

01:07:36.150 --> 01:07:38.060
For $300 tell me the connection

01:07:38.060 --> 01:07:40.523
to the last part of the
stuff that we study.

01:07:42.715 --> 01:07:44.298
- [Student] The last?

01:07:47.668 --> 01:07:49.409
- What's the last thing we talked about

01:07:49.409 --> 01:07:50.242
in the last class?

01:07:50.242 --> 01:07:52.310
- [Student] [Indistinct]

01:07:52.310 --> 01:07:54.991
- Yes, but what was the example, come on?

01:07:54.991 --> 01:07:56.017
- [Student] Rotten apple.

01:07:56.017 --> 01:07:57.993
- No, it's a different apple.

01:08:02.010 --> 01:08:04.293
Boy, that's a short retention period.

01:08:06.300 --> 01:08:10.130
What apple were we talking
about in the last class,

01:08:10.130 --> 01:08:12.488
at the end of the last class?

01:08:12.488 --> 01:08:13.330
- [Student] Like they are fictions.

01:08:13.330 --> 01:08:14.394
- Say again.

01:08:14.394 --> 01:08:15.227
- [Student] Like they are fictions.

01:08:15.227 --> 01:08:19.335
- No, what apple were we talking about?

01:08:19.335 --> 01:08:21.002
- [Student] Influence.

01:08:23.393 --> 01:08:27.060
- We were talking about
apple tree, apple tree.

01:08:28.326 --> 01:08:30.370
[Students] The emanation?

01:08:30.370 --> 01:08:32.835
- Yes, keep going, you're
going to make 300 bucks,

01:08:32.835 --> 01:08:36.280
keep going, keep going.

01:08:36.280 --> 01:08:38.171
There was a tree...

01:08:38.171 --> 01:08:39.014
- [Student] There was a tree

01:08:39.014 --> 01:08:39.847
- Emanated by?..

01:08:39.847 --> 01:08:41.430
- [Student] Emanated by the Buddha.

01:08:41.430 --> 01:08:42.404
- Is it the Buddha?

01:08:42.404 --> 01:08:43.290
- [Student] No.

01:08:43.290 --> 01:08:45.131
- It's not really Buddha

01:08:45.131 --> 01:08:46.048
because you can't climb Buddha

01:08:46.048 --> 01:08:47.163
and pick his tree.

01:08:47.163 --> 01:08:48.320
-[Student] Yes.

01:08:48.320 --> 01:08:52.778
- Then what happened,
what did the tree do?

01:08:52.778 --> 01:08:53.620
- [Student] Made an apple.

01:08:53.620 --> 01:08:55.419
- Apple, and what'd the apple do?

01:08:55.419 --> 01:08:58.303
- Made a worm.

01:08:58.303 --> 01:09:02.556
- How many real trees,
apples and worms are there?

01:09:02.556 --> 01:09:07.556
Zero! Why is that relevant
to a discussion of karma?

01:09:08.000 --> 01:09:11.272
You already got $300, but
somebody can help you.

01:09:11.272 --> 01:09:14.930
Why are we talking about that?

01:09:14.930 --> 01:09:17.525
The other guy said, look if
it's fake, it's not karma

01:09:17.525 --> 01:09:22.525
and result. And we said, all
karmas' results are fake.

01:09:23.080 --> 01:09:27.710
Come on, you're telling
me Buddha can emanate?

01:09:27.710 --> 01:09:30.060
That's also fake but it's real, isn't it?

01:09:30.060 --> 01:09:32.700
You can climb the tree.
You can eat the apple.

01:09:32.700 --> 01:09:35.500
That's why the worm is there.

01:09:35.500 --> 01:09:36.770
What did the tree, the apple,

01:09:36.770 --> 01:09:41.590
and the worm represent in karma?

01:09:41.590 --> 01:09:43.240
What's the three things going on in karma

01:09:43.240 --> 01:09:45.640
similar to the path you haven't walked on,

01:09:45.640 --> 01:09:47.300
similar to the path you walked on,

01:09:47.300 --> 01:09:51.320
similar to the impossible
line between them?

01:09:51.320 --> 01:09:55.843
Somebody does something, it continues,

01:09:57.370 --> 01:10:00.443
and then it opens. Got it?

01:10:00.443 --> 01:10:04.951
Cool, it's all unreal

01:10:04.951 --> 01:10:07.826
but you can use it.

01:10:07.826 --> 01:10:11.520
It's all unreal but you
can use it, that's all.

01:10:11.520 --> 01:10:14.270
When you do the Medicine Buddha mantra

01:10:14.270 --> 01:10:15.490
and you cause...

01:10:15.490 --> 01:10:17.698
and you cure someone's cancer,

01:10:17.698 --> 01:10:18.650
it's totally possible,

01:10:18.650 --> 01:10:21.460
but only if it's empty.

01:10:21.460 --> 01:10:26.009
Only if the energy of the mantra is coming

01:10:26.009 --> 01:10:28.220
from saving life,

01:10:28.220 --> 01:10:31.240
from respecting all life on this planet,

01:10:31.240 --> 01:10:34.400
then you give power to the mantra.

01:10:34.400 --> 01:10:36.580
And then the mantra can
cure somebody's cancer.

01:10:36.580 --> 01:10:40.270
But if you don't understand
that, then the mantra's

01:10:40.270 --> 01:10:45.210
kind of like paper house or something.

01:10:45.210 --> 01:10:48.270
It's there but it's not... Good luck

01:10:48.270 --> 01:10:52.103
if you want to keep the
rain out or something.

01:10:53.500 --> 01:10:56.620
Understand that a mantra is empty,

01:10:56.620 --> 01:10:58.950
and you have to put your karma into it

01:10:58.950 --> 01:11:01.230
and then it will work.

01:11:01.230 --> 01:11:03.780
So, you can't do... sit around do mantras

01:11:03.780 --> 01:11:06.770
without trying to save the environment.

01:11:06.770 --> 01:11:08.540
I mean that's a simple way to help

01:11:08.540 --> 01:11:11.400
80 billion living creatures.

01:11:11.400 --> 01:11:14.580
Right? Plant a tree. Then do your mantras.

01:11:14.580 --> 01:11:18.680
Yay! That would be a real tree.

01:11:18.680 --> 01:11:20.020
So thanks for coming to
the Nagarjuna course.

01:11:20.020 --> 01:11:22.300
I'd like to thank Tim

01:11:22.300 --> 01:11:25.332
for... I don't know, my God,

01:11:25.332 --> 01:11:28.960
he's really a master to get things done.

01:11:28.960 --> 01:11:30.210
I don't know how

01:11:30.210 --> 01:11:31.360
he does all the things he does,

01:11:31.360 --> 01:11:34.085
it's kind of... must be emanation.

01:11:34.085 --> 01:11:35.776
And Pachi and Pau,

01:11:35.776 --> 01:11:38.017
thank you for coming from Mexico

01:11:38.017 --> 01:11:39.492
and helping us to film.

01:11:39.492 --> 01:11:41.690
It makes it fun also.

01:11:41.690 --> 01:11:43.057
It's a lot more fun for me

01:11:43.057 --> 01:11:44.473
if I have more friends here.

01:11:44.473 --> 01:11:47.460
Thank you Rebecca for
coming too from Los Angeles

01:11:47.460 --> 01:11:48.810
to help around the whole thing

01:11:48.810 --> 01:11:51.710
with your great cinematic

01:11:51.710 --> 01:11:53.660
and photographic skills.

01:11:53.660 --> 01:11:57.043
Thank you Venerable
Elly for driving me here

01:11:57.043 --> 01:11:59.243
and paying all my bills,

01:11:59.243 --> 01:12:01.809
especially my student bet bills.

01:12:01.809 --> 01:12:05.230
Thank you Gyelse for Diamond Mountain

01:12:05.230 --> 01:12:08.460
and for keeping this
building in good shape,

01:12:08.460 --> 01:12:10.970
so we can have these classes here.

01:12:10.970 --> 01:12:13.540
Thanks to everybody! And Christina Kasica

01:12:13.540 --> 01:12:17.040
for keeping all our stomachs filled

01:12:17.040 --> 01:12:19.370
during the filming. So
we had a great team here

01:12:19.370 --> 01:12:24.070
and I am really grateful,
and thank you Choney Lama,

01:12:24.070 --> 01:12:27.740
and thank you John Brady
for saving Choney Lama.

01:12:27.740 --> 01:12:31.290
See you guys later! Yay!

